{
  name: "cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"
  // The requirements of the CHERIoT memory subsystem FPV testplan (doc/fpv/README.md),
  // one entry each:
  //   name, desc   the requirement ID and its statement
  //   source      where the rule comes from: !!REGISTER names a register (reggen's
  //               form), a Markdown link names a document section or a key
  //   kind        "spec": a specification states the rule; "RTL": none does, and the
  //               rule follows the design's present behaviour or leaves the outcome
  //               to a specification question
  //   testpoint   its testpoint in cheriot_mem_sys_fpv_testplan.hjson
  //   checks      what decides it: "<check name> (<planned assertion>)"
  //   why         why those checks prove it
  //   milestone   the verification stage of its testpoint: V1, V2 or V2S
  //   priority    the order of work within a stage: "1" before "2"
  //   security    true when a security property depends on it
  //   state       "open" until its checks are proven; with a reason where its checks
  //               decide it only in part
  // The file holds, besides the entries:
  //   written_for   the instance the plan was written for and read against: the
  //                 parameters of Earl Grey (interfaces.md, Parameters)
  //   terms         the words the requirements use, each with its meaning
  //   parameters    the values the instance sets, with the value on Earl Grey
  //   groups        the requirements by feature; a group's conditions say when
  //                 its requirements hold and define its own words
  written_for: "earlgrey"
  terms: [
    {
      name: '''CHERIoT mode'''
      desc: '''The mode enable `cheriot_ena_i` is exactly `MuBi4True`. Any other value, an invalid encoding included, is ePMP mode ([Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram), [Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine); [cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `INTERSIG.MUBI`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Tag path'''
      desc: '''The path that stores and returns the tags: the core's tag filter, the WTRC, the 2:1 tag arbiter and the RMW filter, up to the meta SRAM.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Tag sideband'''
      desc: '''The capability tag carried next to `cored_tl_d`: `cored_tag_h2d` with a request and `cored_tag_d2h` with a response, each a `mubi4_t` ([Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram)). A request's tag sideband is set when it is exactly `MuBi4True`. Any other value, `MuBi4False` or an invalid encoding (neither `MuBi4True` nor `MuBi4False`), is clear ([Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Hinted capability load'''
      desc: '''A read of both words of a capability with the tag sideband set, which asks for the tag ([load_store_unit.rst, Data-Side Memory Interface](hw/vendor/lowrisc_ibex/doc/03_reference/load_store_unit.rst)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''W0, W1'''
      desc: '''The lower and the upper 32-bit word of a capability. The core sends W0 first ([Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Capability store to the NVM'''
      desc: '''A write in CHERIoT mode to the NVM with the tag sideband set ([Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)). The WTRC handles it.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Sweep'''
      desc: '''One run of the revocation engine over `TBRE_NUM_CAPS` capabilities from `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Watch window'''
      desc: '''For one capability of a sweep: from the engine presenting the read of its lower word until its clear is presented. A core write in it keeps its tag ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''TRVK filter'''
      desc: '''The load barrier on the engine's reads: it revokes a tagged, non-sealing capability whose base has its revocation bit set, or whose bitmap lookup fails ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''`fatal_fault`'''
      desc: '''The subsystem's one fatal alert ([Security Alerts](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/interfaces.md#security-alerts)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Tagged region'''
      desc: '''The main SRAM, from `MainSramBaseAddr` up to `MainSramTopAddr`, or the NVM, from `NvmBaseAddr` up to `NvmTopAddr`: the memory that can hold capabilities ([Meta SRAM Address Map](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#meta-sram-address-map)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Meta request'''
      desc: '''A request the tag filter sends on its meta port, to read or to write one tag.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Captured tag'''
      desc: '''The tag a W0 load returns, held by the tag filter for the W1 load that follows ([Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Device port, host port, meta port'''
      desc: '''The three ports of a tag filter. The tag filter receives requests on its device port. It forwards the data half of each access towards memory on its host port, and it sends its meta requests on its meta port. The core's tag filter has `cored_tl_d` as its device port and `cored_tl_h` as its host port. The engine's tag filter has `tbre_tl_h` as its host port.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Meta answer'''
      desc: '''The answer that a tag filter receives on its meta port to a meta request.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Lookup'''
      desc: '''The meta request that a tag filter sends to read the tag of an access.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Meta word'''
      desc: '''A 32-bit word of the meta SRAM.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Bit select'''
      desc: '''The sideband of a meta request that names the bit of the tag within its meta word ([RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Faulty word'''
      desc: '''A word of a capability store to the NVM that is out of sequence or partial, that carries a bad command or data integrity, or whose NVM answer has a bad response integrity.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Owed tag write'''
      desc: '''The tag write of a capability store to the NVM is owed from the cycle in which the NVM answer of W1 arrives, when W0 and W1 both matched, until the meta port accepts the tag write.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Operation'''
      desc: '''A request that the RMW filter accepted, from its acceptance until its answer is taken.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Write-back'''
      desc: '''The full-word write that the RMW filter sends to the meta word that it has read, with only the addressed tag changed.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Fault input'''
      desc: '''A signal on which a block of the subsystem reports a fault to the alert logic, which then requests `fatal_fault`.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Requester ports'''
      desc: '''The four ports that reach the meta SRAM: the tag port (from the RMW filter), `corerevbm_tl` (bitmap reads from the core's TRVK filter), `revbm_tl_d` (software, through `xbar_main`) and the engine's bitmap port, on which the revocation engine's TRVK filter reads the bitmap ([Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram), [Meta SRAM Address Map](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#meta-sram-address-map), [Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers), [Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Tag path access'''
      desc: '''A request on the tag port.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Region of a port'''
      desc: '''The tag port owns both capability tag regions, the NVM capability tags and the main SRAM capability tags, `0x1100_0C00`-`0x1100_97FF`. The other three requester ports own the revocation bitmap, `0x1100_0000`-`0x1100_0BFF` ([Meta SRAM Address Map](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#meta-sram-address-map), column "Reachable from").'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Legal request'''
      desc: '''All four conditions of [Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers) hold: CHERIoT mode; the address inside the port's region; a full 32-bit word at a word-aligned address (`a_size` = 2, so TL-UL sets all four `a_mask` bits: [Request Channel (Channel A)](hw/ip/tlul/doc/TlulProtocolChecker.md#request-channel-channel-a), `sizeMatchesMask`); the opcode `Get` or `PutFullData`.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Error answer'''
      desc: '''The answer an access checker gives a request that is not legal, from its own error responder ([Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Source ID on `meta_sram_tl`'''
      desc: '''The 4:1 arbiter shifts the `a_source` of a request left by two bits and puts the number of the requester port in the two lowest bits. It shifts these bits off again on the `d_source` of the answer ([Usage of Source and Sink ID Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-source-and-sink-id-bits), [Source ID growth](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-growth)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Takes an answer'''
      desc: '''A port takes an answer when it accepts the answer with `d_ready`.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Held request'''
      desc: '''A request that a requester port keeps presenting, unchanged, until it is accepted.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Base'''
      desc: '''The lowest address a capability covers, decoded from its address and its bounds fields (CHERIoT architecture specification v1.0, section 7.13.3 (PDF pages 69-70)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Sealing capability'''
      desc: '''A capability whose permissions are in the sealing format and grant SE, US or U0, the capabilities that the instruction CLC exempts (the CHERIoT architecture specification v1.0, CLC, PDF page 114). The base of a sealing capability is in a namespace of its own, so such a capability is never revoked (CHERIoT architecture specification v1.0, section 7.8 (PDF page 58)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Revocation bit of a base'''
      desc: '''Bit `b` of bitmap word `w`, with `w * 32 + b` = (base - `MainSramBaseAddr`) / 8 ([Meta SRAM Address Map](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#meta-sram-address-map)). The engine uses the bit of the capability's base, not of its address ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine); CHERIoT architecture specification v1.0, section 7.8 (PDF page 58)). For example, base `0x1000_4000` is word 64, bit 0.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Taken start'''
      desc: '''A write of 1 to `TBRE_START` while `TBRE_REGWEN` is 1, in CHERIoT mode, with `TBRE_NUM_CAPS` not zero and `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` in a tagged region ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Ignored start'''
      desc: '''Any other write of 1 to `TBRE_START` while `TBRE_REGWEN` is 1 ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''BASE, NUM'''
      desc: '''The values of `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` and `TBRE_NUM_CAPS` at the start.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Swept capabilities'''
      desc: '''The N capabilities at BASE, BASE + 8,..., with N = min(NUM, (top - BASE) / 8) and top the `MainSramTopAddr` or `NvmTopAddr` of BASE's region ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Active'''
      desc: '''`TBRE_REGWEN` is 0 ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Revoked'''
      desc: '''A swept capability whose tag is set, which is not a sealing capability, whose base lies in the main SRAM region, and whose base's revocation bit is set or whose bitmap lookup failed ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine); [Revoking Capabilities](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#revoking-capabilities)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Touches'''
      desc: '''A core write touches a capability when it is presented on `cored_tl_d`, or accepted there and not yet answered, with its address in the capability's 8 bytes ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Clear'''
      desc: '''The write of tag 0 that the engine presents, through its tag filter, for a revoked capability ([Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)).'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Tracked capability'''
      desc: '''One swept capability that the formal tool chooses freely at the start of a sweep. Any swept capability can be chosen, so a check on the tracked capability covers every swept capability.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Set request'''
      desc: '''The write of 1 that the engine makes into a field of the register file: `TBRE_STATUS.start_err`, `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err` or `INTR_STATE.tbre_done`.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Malformed answer'''
      desc: '''An answer whose `d_opcode` is not the one that its request needs (`AccessAckData` for a `Get`, `AccessAck` for a write), or whose `d_size` differs from the `a_size` of the request.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Fatal state'''
      desc: '''The time from the first failed request or raised fault input after reset until the next reset.'''
    }
    {
      name: '''Test credit, ping credit'''
      desc: '''An alert test sets the test credit and a ping sets the ping credit. The alert event that answers it uses the credit up.'''
    }
  ]
  parameters: [
    {
      name: "MainSramBaseAddr"
      desc: '''Base address of the main SRAM region, inclusive.'''
      value: "0x1000_0000"
    }
    {
      name: "MainSramTopAddr"
      desc: '''Top address of the main SRAM region, exclusive.'''
      value: "0x1003_0000"
    }
    {
      name: "NvmBaseAddr"
      desc: '''Base address of the NVM region, inclusive.'''
      value: "0x3000_0000"
    }
    {
      name: "NvmTopAddr"
      desc: '''Top address of the NVM region, exclusive.'''
      value: "0x3020_0000"
    }
    {
      name: "MetaSramBaseAddr"
      desc: '''Base address of the unified meta SRAM.'''
      value: "0x1100_0000"
    }
    {
      name: "MemSizeRevbm"
      desc: '''Size of the `revbm` window in bytes, set by topgen. Must equal the size of the main SRAM revocation bitmap, which an assertion in the RTL checks.'''
      value: "3072"
    }
    {
      name: "AlertAsyncOn"
      desc: '''Adds synchronizers to the alert sender for an alert handler on another clock, set by topgen.'''
      value: "1'b1"
    }
    {
      name: "AlertSkewCycles"
      desc: '''Cycles of skew tolerated on the differential alert signals, set by topgen.'''
      value: "1"
    }
  ]
  groups: [
    {
      name: '''Tag filter'''
      conditions: [
        '''Every row holds for each access that the core presents, except a capability store to the NVM.'''
        '''The WTRC group covers a capability store to the NVM.'''
        '''For the upper word of a capability whose tag sideband has an invalid encoding, the theory of operation states two tags. The checks of the tag leave that word out, and the plan page lists the case under Out of scope.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01a
          desc: '''Every core access shall be forwarded to the host port.'''
          source: [
            '''[Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["accepted after forwarded (assert_TfForward_AcceptedAfterForwarded)"]
          why: '''The core holds a request until it is accepted. The check allows acceptance no earlier than the cycle in which the host port takes the request. So no accepted request can skip the host port.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01d
          desc: '''No core access shall be forwarded to the host port twice.'''
          source: [
            '''[Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["no extra host request (assert_TfForward_NoExtraHostRequest)"]
          why: '''The check requires each host request to belong to a core request that is not yet forwarded. A second host request for the same core request finds it already forwarded and fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01c
          desc: '''The host port shall carry no request that the core did not present.'''
          source: [
            '''[Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["no extra host request (assert_TfForward_NoExtraHostRequest)"]
          why: '''A host request that belongs to no core request fails the check. The check looks at every host request that is presented, so it also catches a request that the host port never takes.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01b
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry the core access's address unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the host request to carry the core request's address in the cycle it is forwarded. Any changed bit fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01e
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry the core access's opcode unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the host request to carry the core request's opcode in the cycle it is forwarded. A read turned into a write, or the reverse, fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01f
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry the core access's size unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the host request to carry the core request's size. A changed size fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01g
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry the core access's byte mask unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the host request to carry the core request's mask. A byte added to or dropped from a store fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01h
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry the core access's data unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the host request to carry the core request's data. Any changed bit fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01i
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry the core access's source ID (`a_source`) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the host request to carry the core request's `a_source`. A changed ID fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_01j
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry the core access's user bits (`a_user`, with its integrity) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the host request to carry the core request's `a_user`, its integrity included. Any changed bit fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_02a
          desc: '''In CHERIoT mode, a 64-bit-aligned read to a tagged region that the core hints as a capability load shall issue a meta request.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
            '''[cheriot.rst, Data Memory Tag Interface](hw/vendor/lowrisc_ibex/doc/03_reference/cheriot.rst)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_lookup"
          checks: ["lookup in same cycle (assert_TfLookup_LookupInSameCycle)"]
          why: '''The check requires a meta request for every request that needs a lookup. A hinted aligned read to a tagged region in CHERIoT mode needs one, so a missing lookup fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_02b
          desc: '''In CHERIoT mode, a 64-bit-aligned hinted read to a tagged region shall issue at most one meta request.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_lookup"
          checks: ["no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)"]
          why: '''The check accepts one meta request for each read that needs a lookup. A second meta request for the same read fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_03a
          desc: '''In CHERIoT mode, a write to a tagged region shall issue a meta request.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
            '''[Datapath](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#datapath)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_lookup"
          checks: ["lookup in same cycle (assert_TfLookup_LookupInSameCycle)"]
          why: '''A write to a tagged region in CHERIoT mode needs a lookup, so the check requires its meta request.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_03b
          desc: '''In CHERIoT mode, a write to a tagged region shall issue at most one meta request.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_lookup"
          checks: ["no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)"]
          why: '''The check accepts one meta request for each write that needs a lookup. A second meta request for the same write fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_04a
          desc: '''In ePMP mode, no access shall issue a meta request.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `MODE_GATING`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `INTERSIG.MUBI`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_lookup"
          checks: ["no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)"]
          why: '''In ePMP mode no request needs a lookup, so any meta request fails the check. The check covers each of the 15 values of the mode enable that select ePMP mode.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_04b
          desc: '''In CHERIoT mode, an access that is neither an aligned hinted read nor a write to a tagged region shall issue no meta request.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_lookup"
          checks: ["no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)"]
          why: '''A plain read, a W1 read and an access outside the tagged regions need no lookup, so a meta request for one of them fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_05a
          desc: '''A meta request shall address the meta word that holds the tag of the 8-byte location containing the access address.'''
          source: [
            '''[Metadata Encoding](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#metadata-encoding)'''
            '''[Meta SRAM Address Map](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#meta-sram-address-map)'''
            '''No specification states the bit order of the tags within a meta word.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_meta_request"
          checks: ["tag word and bit (assert_TfMetaRequest_TagWordAndBit)"]
          why: '''The check computes from the request's address the meta word that holds its tag, and compares it with the meta request's address. A meta request to another word fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_05b
          desc: '''A meta request's bit select shall name the bit, within the meta word, of the 8-byte location containing the access address.'''
          source: [
            '''[Metadata Encoding](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#metadata-encoding)'''
            '''No specification states the bit order of the tags within a meta word.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_meta_request"
          checks: ["tag word and bit (assert_TfMetaRequest_TagWordAndBit)"]
          why: '''The check computes from the request's address the bit that holds its tag, and compares it with the bit select. A bit select that names a neighbouring bit fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_06a
          desc: '''A write with the tag sideband clear shall ask for tag 0.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TAG_CLEAR_ON_DATA_WRITE`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''CHERIoT architecture specification v1.0, section 7.7'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_meta_request"
          checks: ["write carries its tag (assert_TfMetaRequest_WriteCarriesItsTag)", "Get only for a read (assert_TfMetaRequest_GetOnlyForARead)"]
          why: '''The first check compares the tag to write with the tag sideband, which is 0 for a plain store. The second check requires the meta request to be a write, so the RMW filter writes the 0.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_06b
          desc: '''A write with the tag sideband set shall ask for tag 1.'''
          source: [
            '''[Inter-Module Signals](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/interfaces.md#inter-module-signals)'''
            '''[cheriot.rst, Data Memory Tag Interface](hw/vendor/lowrisc_ibex/doc/03_reference/cheriot.rst)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_meta_request"
          checks: ["write carries its tag (assert_TfMetaRequest_WriteCarriesItsTag)", "Get only for a read (assert_TfMetaRequest_GetOnlyForARead)"]
          why: '''For a capability store, whose tag sideband is set, the first check requires tag 1. The second check requires the meta request to be a write.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_06c
          desc: '''A write whose tag sideband holds an invalid encoding shall ask for tag 0.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_meta_request"
          checks: ["write carries its tag (assert_TfMetaRequest_WriteCarriesItsTag)", "Get only for a read (assert_TfMetaRequest_GetOnlyForARead)"]
          why: '''The first check reads the sideband at `cored_tag_h2d` and expects tag 0 for every value but `MuBi4True`. A design that reads an invalid encoding as set, for example by testing one bit, writes tag 1 and fails it. The W1 to the NVM after a tagged W0 is left out: the specification states two tags for it. A main SRAM W1 is checked for tag 0.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_07a
          desc: '''A response to the core shall carry its host response's opcode.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["answer has host fields (assert_TfForward_AnswerHasHostFields)"]
          why: '''The check compares the answer's `d_opcode` with that of the host answer it joins. A changed opcode fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_07b
          desc: '''A response to the core shall carry its host response's size.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["answer has host fields (assert_TfForward_AnswerHasHostFields)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer to carry the host answer's `d_size`. A changed size fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_07c
          desc: '''A response to the core shall carry its host response's source ID (`d_source`).'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["answer has host fields (assert_TfForward_AnswerHasHostFields)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer to carry the host answer's `d_source`. An answer joined to the wrong host answer, or with a changed ID, fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_07d
          desc: '''A response to the core shall carry its host response's data.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["answer has host fields (assert_TfForward_AnswerHasHostFields)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer to carry the host answer's `d_data`. Another request's data fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_07e
          desc: '''A response to the core shall carry its host response's data integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["answer has host fields (assert_TfForward_AnswerHasHostFields)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer to carry the host answer's data integrity. Any change fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_07f
          desc: '''A response to the core shall carry its host response's response integrity, when no meta error is merged in.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["answer has host fields (assert_TfForward_AnswerHasHostFields)"]
          why: '''With no meta error merged in, the check requires the answer to carry the host answer's response integrity. With a meta error merged in, the testpoint `tf_errors` checks the response integrity.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_08
          desc: '''A read response without an error, to a request that made a meta request, shall carry the tag of its meta response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
            '''[load_store_unit.rst, Protocol](hw/vendor/lowrisc_ibex/doc/03_reference/load_store_unit.rst)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)"]
          why: '''For W0 of a capability load without `d_error`, the check expects the tag of the meta response. Any other tag fails the check. The check does not look at the tag of a response with `d_error`.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_09
          desc: '''After the response to an aligned read, the next response to an unaligned read shall carry the captured tag.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
            '''[cheriot.rst, Data Memory Tag Interface](hw/vendor/lowrisc_ibex/doc/03_reference/cheriot.rst)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)"]
          why: '''For the W1 after a W0, the check expects the captured tag. A lost or changed tag fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_10
          desc: '''The captured tag shall be cleared after the unaligned read response that carries it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)"]
          why: '''The check expects tag 0 on a plain load of the upper word immediately after a capability load with tag 1. A captured tag that is not cleared returns tag 1 and fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_11a
          desc: '''A write response shall be untagged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)"]
          why: '''For a write, the check expects tag 0. A tagged write answer fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_11b
          desc: '''A write response shall leave the captured tag unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)"]
          why: '''A write answered between W0 and W1 must not change the tag that W1 receives. On the core's tag filter the case cannot occur, because the core sends W1 immediately after W0. On the engine's tag filter it occurs when the engine clears a tag, and the same check decides it there (the revocation engine checker).'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_11c
          desc: '''A read response shall be untagged unless its request was a hinted capability load to a tagged region in CHERIoT mode.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot.rst, Data Memory Tag Interface](hw/vendor/lowrisc_ibex/doc/03_reference/cheriot.rst)'''
            '''CHERIoT architecture specification v1.0, section 7.7'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)"]
          why: '''For a plain load, a load outside the tagged regions and a load in ePMP mode, the check expects tag 0. A tag of 1 fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_11d
          desc: '''A read response to a request whose tag sideband holds an invalid encoding shall be untagged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)"]
          why: '''A read with an invalid tag sideband is not hinted, so the check expects tag 0. A design that takes an invalid encoding as the hint returns the stored tag 1 and fails the check. The W1 of a load is left out: the specification states two tags for it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_12a
          desc: '''`d_error` towards the core shall be set when the host response has an error.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_errors"
          checks: ["error when a part has one (assert_TfErrors_ErrorWhenAPartHasOne)"]
          why: '''When the host answer has `d_error`, the check requires `d_error` on the answer to the core. A lost error fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_12c
          desc: '''`d_error` towards the core shall be set when the meta response has an error.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_errors"
          checks: ["error when a part has one (assert_TfErrors_ErrorWhenAPartHasOne)"]
          why: '''When the joined meta answer has an error, the check requires `d_error` on the answer to the core. A lost tag error fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_12b
          desc: '''`d_error` towards the core shall be clear when neither the host nor the meta response has an error.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_errors"
          checks: ["no error without a cause (assert_TfErrors_NoErrorWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''An answer to the core with `d_error` and no error in either part fails the check. Its parts are the host answer and, if a lookup was made, the joined meta answer.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_13a
          desc: '''When a meta error sets `d_error` on an error-free host response, a valid response integrity shall stay valid.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_errors"
          checks: ["merged error keeps integrity (assert_TfErrors_MergedErrorKeepsIntegrity)"]
          why: '''When the host integrity is valid and only the meta answer has an error, the check requires a valid response integrity. A design that breaks the valid integrity fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_13b
          desc: '''When a meta error sets `d_error` on an error-free host response, an invalid response integrity shall stay invalid.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_errors"
          checks: ["merged error keeps integrity (assert_TfErrors_MergedErrorKeepsIntegrity)"]
          why: '''When the host integrity is broken and only the meta answer has an error, the check requires the response integrity to stay broken. A design that makes the broken integrity valid fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_14
          desc: '''The meta port shall always accept a meta response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_flow"
          checks: ["meta answer taken (assert_TfFlow_MetaAnswerTaken)"]
          why: '''The check looks at every cycle with a meta answer offered. One cycle with `d_ready` at 0 fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_15a
          desc: '''The tag filter shall eventually accept every request, provided that at most two requests are outstanding and that the host port and the meta port accept requests.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_flow"
          checks: ["request eventually accepted (assert_TfFlow_RequestEventuallyAccepted)"]
          why: '''The formal tool searches for a run in which a request waits forever while the host port and the meta port keep accepting requests. Such a run fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_15b
          desc: '''The tag filter shall eventually answer every accepted request, provided that the host port and the meta port answer.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_flow"
          checks: ["request eventually answered (assert_TfFlow_RequestEventuallyAnswered)"]
          why: '''The formal tool searches for a run in which an accepted request is never answered while the host port and the meta port keep answering. Such a run fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_15c
          desc: '''The tag filter shall answer no request twice.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_flow"
          checks: ["no extra answer (assert_TfFlow_NoExtraAnswer)"]
          why: '''The check allows one answer for each accepted request, so a second answer fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_16a
          desc: '''A request shall reach the host port in the cycle the core presents it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the host request in the cycle the core presents it. Any delay fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_16c
          desc: '''A request that needs a lookup shall reach the meta port in the cycle the core presents it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_lookup"
          checks: ["lookup in same cycle (assert_TfLookup_LookupInSameCycle)"]
          why: '''The check requires the meta request in the cycle the core presents the request.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_16b
          desc: '''A response shall reach the core in the cycle its last part arrives. Its parts are the host response and, when its request made a meta request, the meta response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_forward"
          checks: ["answer on last part (assert_TfForward_AnswerOnLastPart)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer to the core in the cycle its last part arrives. Its parts are the host answer and, if a lookup was made, the meta answer. An early or late answer fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_17
          desc: '''Every meta request the tag filter generates shall carry a valid command integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Description](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/README.md#description)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `BUS.INTEGRITY`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_lookup"
          checks: ["lookup carries valid integrity (assert_TfLookup_LookupCarriesValidIntegrity)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the command integrity of every meta request. No other check covers it, because the TL-UL assertion-based verification IP (ABVIP) checks no integrity field.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_18a
          desc: '''A tagged response to the core shall carry `MuBi4True` on `cored_tag_d2h`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram)'''
            '''[Capability Tag Sideband](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/rv_core_ibex/doc/theory_of_operation.md#capability-tag-sideband)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)"]
          why: '''The check reads tag 1 only from `MuBi4True` on `cored_tag_d2h`. A tagged answer sent as `MuBi4False` or as an invalid encoding reads as 0 and fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TF_18b
          desc: '''An untagged response to the core without `d_error` shall carry `MuBi4False` on `cored_tag_d2h`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram)'''
            '''[Capability Tag Sideband](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/rv_core_ibex/doc/theory_of_operation.md#capability-tag-sideband)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tf_sticky_tag"
          checks: ["untagged answer carries MuBi4False (assert_TfStickyTag_UntaggedAnswerCarriesMuBi4False)"]
          why: '''The check compares `cored_tag_d2h` of every untagged answer without `d_error` with `MuBi4False`. An invalid encoding, which the core also reads as 0, fails it. The requirement and the check both leave out an answer with `d_error`.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''WTRC'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows apply to a capability store to the NVM and to the requests around it.'''
        '''Every other access passes the WTRC unchanged, and the Tag filter rows cover it with the WTRC in place.'''
        '''The WTRC tracks the capability being stored, and it treats a word as out of sequence in four cases ([Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)).'''
        '''Case 1: a W1 arrives while the WTRC tracks no capability.'''
        '''Case 2: after a W0, any request arrives that is not the W1 of the same capability.'''
        '''Case 3: any request arrives after a W1 and before that W1 is answered or its tag write is issued.'''
        '''Case 4: after the tag write of a W1 is issued, a W1 arrives, or a W0 arrives before that W1 is answered.'''
        '''A word is matched when its NVM read succeeded, it is a full-word `PutFullData` in sequence, and its data and data integrity equal those of the NVM answer ([Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)).'''
        '''The checks decide the rows on a faulty word for every faulty word, also after an earlier one.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_01
          desc: '''A capability store to the NVM shall reach the host port only as a `Get` of the word it targets, never as a write.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["sent as a full-word Get (assert_WtrcStore_SentAsAFullWordGet)"]
          why: '''The check requires a `Get` on the host port for every word of a capability store to the NVM. A write reaching the NVM fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_02
          desc: '''The `Get` that a capability store to the NVM becomes shall carry a valid command integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["Get has valid command integrity (assert_WtrcStore_GetHasValidCommandIntegrity)"]
          why: '''For a capability store to the NVM, the check recomputes the `Get`'s command integrity. The store's own integrity, left on the `Get`, fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_03a
          desc: '''W0 of a capability store to the NVM shall issue no meta request.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["no lookup for a capability store (assert_WtrcStore_NoLookupForACapabilityStore)"]
          why: '''Any meta request presented for W0 of a capability store to the NVM fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_03b
          desc: '''W1 of a capability store to the NVM shall issue no meta request other than its tag write.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["no lookup for a capability store (assert_WtrcStore_NoLookupForACapabilityStore)"]
          why: '''For W1 of a capability store to the NVM, the check allows only the tag write. Any other meta request fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_04a
          desc: '''W0 shall be answered with `d_error` when it did not match.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["W0 error on mismatch (assert_WtrcCompare_W0ErrorOnMismatch)", "answer after NVM answer (assert_WtrcCompare_AnswerAfterNvmAnswer)"]
          why: '''The first check requires `d_error` on every W0 that did not match. The second check requires W0 to wait for the NVM answer that decides whether it matched.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_04b
          desc: '''W0 shall be answered without `d_error` when it matched.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["W0 error on mismatch (assert_WtrcCompare_W0ErrorOnMismatch)"]
          why: '''The check requires W0's answer to have `d_error` exactly when W0 did not match. It works in both directions, so a matched W0 answered with `d_error` fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_05a
          desc: '''Each word of a capability store to the NVM shall be answered once.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["no extra answer (assert_TfFlow_NoExtraAnswer)", "request eventually answered (assert_TfFlow_RequestEventuallyAnswered)"]
          why: '''The tag filter checks count the answers to every request, a capability store included. The first check allows at most one answer, and the second check requires that one answer eventually arrives.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_05b
          desc: '''Each word of a capability store to the NVM shall be answered with an `AccessAck`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["untagged AccessAck answer (assert_WtrcStore_UntaggedAccessAckAnswer)"]
          why: '''For each word of a capability store to the NVM, the check compares the answer's opcode with `AccessAck`. Any other opcode fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_05c
          desc: '''Each word of a capability store to the NVM shall be answered untagged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["untagged AccessAck answer (assert_WtrcStore_UntaggedAccessAckAnswer)"]
          why: '''For each word of a capability store to the NVM, the check requires tag 0 on the answer. A tagged answer fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_05d
          desc: '''Each word of a capability store to the NVM shall be answered with its request's `a_source` as `d_source`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["untagged AccessAck answer (assert_WtrcStore_UntaggedAccessAckAnswer)"]
          why: '''For each word of a capability store to the NVM, the check compares the answer's `d_source` with the word's `a_source`. Another ID fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_05e
          desc: '''Each word of a capability store to the NVM shall be answered with a valid response integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["untagged AccessAck answer (assert_WtrcStore_UntaggedAccessAckAnswer)"]
          why: '''For each word of a capability store to the NVM, the check recomputes the answer's response integrity. A broken one fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_06a
          desc: '''When W0 and W1 both matched, W1's NVM answer shall be turned into one tag write of tag 1 to the capability's tag bit.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
            '''No specification states the bit order of the tags within a meta word.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["only the owed tag write (assert_WtrcCompare_OnlyTheOwedTagWrite)", "W1 answered after tag write (assert_WtrcCompare_W1AnsweredAfterTagWrite)"]
          why: '''The first check requires the tag write to carry tag 1 to the right word and bit. The second check requires W1 to be answered only after the tag write is answered, so the tag write must be issued.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_06b
          desc: '''W1's tag write shall be issued only after W1's NVM read has returned.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["only the owed tag write (assert_WtrcCompare_OnlyTheOwedTagWrite)", "no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)"]
          why: '''A tag write is owed only from the cycle W1's NVM answer arrives. Before then the lookup check applies, and a tag write belongs to no request that needs a lookup, so the lookup check fails.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_06c
          desc: '''W1's tag write shall reach the meta port before any later lookup.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["only the owed tag write (assert_WtrcCompare_OnlyTheOwedTagWrite)"]
          why: '''While the tag write is owed, the only meta request allowed is the tag write. A lookup presented before the owed tag write fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_07a
          desc: '''W1 shall be answered with `d_error` when the tag write's answer has `d_error`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["W1 answered after tag write (assert_WtrcCompare_W1AnsweredAfterTagWrite)"]
          why: '''The check requires W1's `d_error` to equal that of the tag write's answer. A lost error fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_07b
          desc: '''W1 shall be answered without `d_error` when the tag write's answer has none.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["W1 answered after tag write (assert_WtrcCompare_W1AnsweredAfterTagWrite)"]
          why: '''The check requires W1's `d_error` to equal that of the tag write's answer. An added error fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_08a
          desc: '''When W0 or W1 did not match, W1 shall be answered with `d_error`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["W1 error on mismatch (assert_WtrcCompare_W1ErrorOnMismatch)"]
          why: '''When W0 or W1 did not match, the check requires `d_error` on W1.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_08b
          desc: '''When W0 or W1 did not match, no tag write shall be issued.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["W1 error on mismatch (assert_WtrcCompare_W1ErrorOnMismatch)", "no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)"]
          why: '''After a mismatch no tag write is owed, so the lookup check applies. A tag write then belongs to no request that needs a lookup, and the lookup check fails.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_09
          desc: '''A capability store to the NVM that fails only because its NVM read failed or its data or data integrity differ from those that the NVM read returned shall raise no alert.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_compare"
          checks: ["no alert without a cause (assert_WtrcCompare_NoAlertWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''The check allows the WTRC's fault input to the alert to rise only after a faulty word has occurred since reset. A mismatch or a failed NVM read is not a faulty word, so an alert for it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_10a
          desc: '''A faulty word shall be answered with `d_error`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["faulty word answered with error (assert_WtrcFaults_FaultyWordAnsweredWithError)"]
          why: '''The check requires `d_error` on the answer to every faulty word, whatever came before it. A faulty word is a word with a bad integrity, a partial word or a word out of sequence. An answer to a faulty word without `d_error` fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_10b
          desc: '''A faulty word shall write no tag.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["tag write only for matched pair (assert_WtrcFaults_TagWriteOnlyForMatchedPair)"]
          why: '''A faulty word never matches, so the check allows no tag write for a W1 whose pair, that W1 and its W0, holds a faulty word. A tag write after a faulty word of that pair fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_11
          desc: '''A faulty word shall raise `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["faulty word raises alert (assert_WtrcFaults_FaultyWordRaisesAlert)"]
          why: '''No specification states how soon the alert follows the fault, so the check has no time bound. It needs no fairness, because nothing outside the design holds the alert back.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_12
          desc: '''Any other request out of the sequence of a capability store to the NVM shall raise `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["other request out of sequence raises alert (assert_WtrcFaults_OtherRequestOutOfSequenceRaisesAlert)"]
          why: '''The check looks at every load or store that is not a capability store. When such a request is out of sequence, the check requires the alert request after it. A design that lets such a request pass without the alert fails it. No specification states how soon the alert follows, so the check has no time bound, and it needs no fairness.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_13a
          desc: '''Every access that is not a capability store to the NVM shall pass the WTRC unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The tag filter checks cover every access that is not a capability store to the NVM, with the WTRC in place. So a field that the WTRC changes on such an access fails them.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_13b
          desc: '''Every access that is not a capability store to the NVM shall pass the WTRC with unchanged timing.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_store"
          checks: ["forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)", "answer on last part (assert_TfForward_AnswerOnLastPart)"]
          why: '''With the WTRC in place, these checks require the host request in the cycle the core presents the request, and the answer in the cycle its last part arrives. A cycle added by the WTRC fails them.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_14a
          desc: '''The answer to an access that is not a capability store to the NVM shall pass the WTRC unchanged, also while a capability is open and when the access is out of sequence.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["other answer passes unchanged (assert_WtrcFaults_OtherAnswerPassesUnchanged)"]
          why: '''For an access that is not a capability store word, the check compares the core's answer with the host answer field by field, also after a request out of sequence. A field that the WTRC changes fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_14b
          desc: '''The answer to an access that is not a capability store to the NVM shall reach the core as the answer to that access, in the order of the core's requests, also while a capability is open and when the access is out of sequence.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
            '''[load_store_unit.rst, Protocol](hw/vendor/lowrisc_ibex/doc/03_reference/load_store_unit.rst)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["answer goes to its own access (assert_WtrcFaults_AnswerGoesToItsOwnAccess)"]
          why: '''The check pairs each answer with the oldest unanswered core request and with that request's own lookup answer. A load whose lookup answer overtakes the answer to W1's tag write, and that receives the tag write's answer, fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_15
          desc: '''A capability store to the NVM whose W0 is taken after the answer to the W1 of the previous capability, with no other capability store word between its W0 and its W1, and whose W0 and W1 both match, shall be turned into its tag write, whatever requests came before its W0.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["matched store after fault sets tag (assert_WtrcFaults_MatchedStoreAfterFaultSetsTag)", "store W1 answered (assert_WtrcFaults_StoreW1Answered)"]
          why: '''The first check requires the tag write's answer before W1's answer, whatever came before W0. A design that stays in a fault state answers W1 without a tag write and fails the first check. A design that never answers W1 passes the first check and fails _store W1 answered_.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_16
          desc: '''The WTRC shall issue a tag write only for a W1 whose capability a W0 of the same capability opened, with no other W0 taken between them, when that W0 and that W1 both matched.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["tag write only for matched pair (assert_WtrcFaults_TagWriteOnlyForMatchedPair)"]
          why: '''The check finds the W1 and the W0 that each tag write belongs to. A tag write fails the check when it is for a W1 whose capability another W0 opened, or when it comes after a second W0, or when it is for a pair with a word that did not match.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WTRC_17
          desc: '''A capability store to the NVM whose W0 is taken after the answer to the W1 of the previous capability, with no other capability store word between its W0 and its W1, and whose W0 or W1 does not match, shall receive `d_error` on W1's answer, whatever requests came before its W0.'''
          source: [
            '''[Write-to-Read-and-Compare Filter (WTRC)](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#write-to-read-and-compare-filter-wtrc)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wtrc_faults"
          checks: ["unmatched store after fault errors (assert_WtrcFaults_UnmatchedStoreAfterFaultErrors)", "store W1 answered (assert_WtrcFaults_StoreW1Answered)"]
          why: '''The first check requires `d_error` on W1's answer, whatever came before W0, and _tag write only for matched pair_ forbids its tag write. A design that answers W1 without `d_error`, or never answers it, fails.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''2:1 tag arbiter'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows apply to both inputs of the arbiter: the core's tag filter and the engine's tag filter.'''
        '''The Sweep and Decision and clears groups cover what the engine asks for.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_01a
          desc: '''Every request accepted on either input shall be forwarded to the RMW filter.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check requires the forwarded request in the cycle the input request is accepted. A dropped request fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_01b
          desc: '''No accepted request shall be forwarded to the RMW filter twice.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["from the named input (assert_ArbForward_FromTheNamedInput)"]
          why: '''The check requires each forwarded request to match an input request accepted in the same cycle. A second copy in a later cycle matches none and fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_02
          desc: '''No request shall be forwarded that neither input presented.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["from the named input (assert_ArbForward_FromTheNamedInput)"]
          why: '''A forwarded request that matches no input request fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_03a
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry its input's address unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[Source ID requirements for bus primitives](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-bus-primitives)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded address with the input request's address. Any change fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_03b
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry its input's opcode unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[Source ID requirements for bus primitives](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-bus-primitives)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded opcode with the input request's opcode. A changed opcode fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_03c
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry its input's size unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[Source ID requirements for bus primitives](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-bus-primitives)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded size with the input request's size. A changed size fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_03d
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry its input's byte mask unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[Source ID requirements for bus primitives](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-bus-primitives)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded mask with the input request's mask. A changed mask fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_03e
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry its input's data unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[Source ID requirements for bus primitives](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-bus-primitives)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded data with the input request's data. A changed bit fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_03f
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry its input's user bits (`a_user`, with its integrity) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[Source ID requirements for bus primitives](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-bus-primitives)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded `a_user` with the input request's `a_user`. Any change fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_04a
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry its input's tag.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded tag with that of the input it came from. The other input's tag fails it. The check covers two inputs that present different tags in the same cycle.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_04b
          desc: '''A forwarded request shall carry its input's bit select.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded bit select with that of its input. The other input's bit select fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_05a
          desc: '''Every answer shall go to the input whose request it answers.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["taken with its input (assert_ArbReturn_TakenWithItsInput)"]
          why: '''The RMW filter's answer may be taken only when its own input takes it. An answer lost on the way is taken by no input and fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_05b
          desc: '''No answer shall go to the input whose request it does not answer.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["answer to its input (assert_ArbReturn_AnswerToItsInput)"]
          why: '''An answer at an input whose number is not bit 0 of `d_source` fails the check, and so does an answer at both inputs.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_06
          desc: '''An answer shall carry, as `d_source`, the `a_source` its input sent.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID growth](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-growth)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["source shifted back (assert_ArbReturn_SourceShiftedBack)", "keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)"]
          why: '''On the way out the arbiter shifts `a_source` left to add a bit that names the input. The shift drops the top bit of the requester's `a_source`. The RMW filter returns the ID unchanged, and the check of `arb_return` requires the added bit to be removed on the way back. So the requester receives the `a_source` it sent if that top bit is 0.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_07a
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its input with its opcode unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_ArbReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer at the input to keep the RMW filter's opcode. Any change fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_07b
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its input with its size unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_ArbReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer at the input to keep the RMW filter's size. Any change fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_07c
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its input with its data unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_ArbReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer at the input to keep the RMW filter's data. Any change fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_07d
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its input with its error bit (`d_error`) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_ArbReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the RMW filter's `d_error` at the input. A hidden or invented error fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_07e
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its input with its user bits (`d_user`, with its integrity) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_ArbReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer at the input to keep the RMW filter's `d_user`. Any change fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_07f
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its input with its tag unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_ArbReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer at the input to keep the RMW filter's tag. A changed tag fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_08
          desc: '''A request held on either input shall eventually be accepted, provided that the RMW filter keeps accepting requests.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[`tlul_socket_m1`](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#tlul_socket_m1)'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "arb_flow"
          checks: ["no starvation (assert_ArbFlow_NoStarvation)"]
          why: '''The formal tool searches for a run in which one input waits forever while the other keeps winning. Such a run fails the check. The check covers the case in which the engine's tag filter presents a request in every cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: the arbitration policy is not stated by a specification"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_09
          desc: '''A request presented while the other input presents none shall reach the RMW filter in the same cycle.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_flow"
          checks: ["alone in same cycle (assert_ArbFlow_AloneInSameCycle)"]
          why: '''The check requires the request at the RMW filter in the cycle it is presented. Any delay fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_10
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its input in the cycle the RMW filter gives it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_flow"
          checks: ["answer at once (assert_ArbFlow_AnswerAtOnce)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer at its input in the cycle the RMW filter sends it. A delay fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ARB_11
          desc: '''A request from the core's tag filter shall reach the RMW filter exactly as the arbiter forwards it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "arb_forward"
          checks: ["core request unchanged (assert_ArbForward_CoreRequestUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares the request at the RMW filter with the arbiter's output. Any change by the logic between the arbiter and the RMW filter fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''RMW filter'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows apply to every request that the 2:1 tag arbiter forwards, whether it is a read or a write.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_01
          desc: '''A read shall be forwarded to the meta SRAM at its meta word address.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_read"
          checks: ["Get of its meta word (assert_RmwRead_GetOfItsMetaWord)"]
          why: '''The check compares the `Get`'s address with the read's meta word. A `Get` of another word fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_02
          desc: '''A read's response without `d_error` shall return, as the tag, the bit of the response word that its bit select names.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[load_store_unit.rst, Protocol](hw/vendor/lowrisc_ibex/doc/03_reference/load_store_unit.rst)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_read"
          checks: ["returns its tag bit (assert_RmwRead_ReturnsItsTagBit)"]
          why: '''The check picks the bit out of the word read and compares it with the answer's tag. Another bit fails it. The check covers words whose neighbouring bits all differ from that bit. It does not look at the tag of an answer with `d_error`.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_03
          desc: '''A write shall first issue a full-word `Get` of its meta word.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_skip"
          checks: ["full-word Get first (assert_RmwWriteSkip_FullWordGetFirst)", "answer after Get answer (assert_RmwWriteSkip_AnswerAfterGetAnswer)"]
          why: '''The first check requires a full-word `Get` as the write's first request. The second check requires that the write is not answered before its `Get` is answered.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_04
          desc: '''A write whose tag equals the stored bit shall issue no write-back.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_skip"
          checks: ["no write-back (assert_RmwWriteSkip_NoWriteBack)"]
          why: '''A write-back presented when the bit already equals the tag fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_05
          desc: '''A write with no write-back shall be answered with an `AccessAck`.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_skip"
          checks: ["answered with AccessAck (assert_RmwWriteSkip_AnsweredWithAccessAck)", "answer after Get answer (assert_RmwWriteSkip_AnswerAfterGetAnswer)"]
          why: '''For a write whose bit already equals the tag, the first check compares the answer's opcode with `AccessAck`. The second check requires the answer to come only after the `Get` answer has arrived.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_06a
          desc: '''A write whose tag differs from the stored bit shall write back the read word with that bit set to the tag.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_back"
          checks: ["carries the updated word (assert_RmwWriteBack_CarriesTheUpdatedWord)"]
          why: '''The check sets the selected bit of the word read to the tag and compares the result with the write-back. A bit not set to the tag fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_06b
          desc: '''A write-back shall leave every other bit of the read word unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_back"
          checks: ["carries the updated word (assert_RmwWriteBack_CarriesTheUpdatedWord)"]
          why: '''The check compares all 32 bits of the write-back with the word read, with its selected bit set to the tag. A change to any other bit fails it. The check covers neighbouring bits at 0 and at 1.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_07a
          desc: '''The write-back shall be a full-word `PutFullData` to the same meta word.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_back"
          checks: ["full-word Put to same word (assert_RmwWriteBack_FullWordPutToSameWord)"]
          why: '''The check compares the opcode, the size, the mask and the address with a full-word write to the word read. Any difference fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_07b
          desc: '''The write-back shall carry a freshly computed command integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_back"
          checks: ["full-word Put to same word (assert_RmwWriteBack_FullWordPutToSameWord)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the write-back's command integrity. The `Get`'s integrity left in place fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_07c
          desc: '''The write-back shall carry a freshly computed data integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_back"
          checks: ["full-word Put to same word (assert_RmwWriteBack_FullWordPutToSameWord)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the data integrity over the word written back. The integrity of the word read fails it, because one bit changed.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_08
          desc: '''The write-back's response shall be forwarded as the write's response.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_back"
          checks: ["write-back answer passed up (assert_RmwWriteBack_WriteBackAnswerPassedUp)"]
          why: '''The check requires the write's answer in the cycle of the write-back's answer, with its opcode and error. An answer taken from the `Get` fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_09
          desc: '''Every request issued for a write shall carry the write's `a_source`.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_write_back"
          checks: ["keeps the write's source (assert_RmwWriteBack_KeepsTheWritesSource)"]
          why: '''The check requires the write's `a_source` on the `Get` and on the write-back. Another ID fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_10
          desc: '''A new request shall be accepted only in one of two kinds of cycle. In the first, no operation is unanswered. In the second, the only unanswered operation is a read, and that read is answered in the same cycle.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_single_op"
          checks: ["one operation at a time (assert_RmwSingleOp_OneOperationAtATime)"]
          why: '''A request accepted while an earlier operation is still unanswered fails the check, unless that operation is a read answered in the same cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_11
          desc: '''A read presented in the cycle the previous read is answered shall be accepted in that cycle, if the meta SRAM side is ready.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_read"
          checks: ["back-to-back read accepted (assert_RmwRead_BackToBackReadAccepted)"]
          why: '''The check requires the next read to be accepted in the cycle the previous one is answered. A cycle lost fails it.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_13
          desc: '''A device error on the `Get` of a write shall abort the write, so that the write issues no write-back.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_errors"
          checks: ["Get error stops the write (assert_RmwErrors_GetErrorStopsTheWrite)"]
          why: '''A write-back presented after a `Get` answer with `d_error` fails the check, whether or not the bit differs.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_14
          desc: '''A device error on a meta SRAM response shall be answered upstream with `d_error`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_errors"
          checks: ["error passed up (assert_RmwErrors_ErrorPassedUp)"]
          why: '''The check requires `d_error` upstream for every operation with an error from the meta SRAM. A lost error fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_15a
          desc: '''Every accepted request shall eventually be answered, provided that the meta SRAM answers.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_single_op"
          checks: ["every operation answered (assert_RmwSingleOp_EveryOperationAnswered)"]
          why: '''The formal tool searches for a run in which an operation is never answered while the meta SRAM answers. Such a run fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_15b
          desc: '''No accepted request shall be answered twice.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_single_op"
          checks: ["one answer per operation (assert_RmwSingleOp_OneAnswerPerOperation)"]
          why: '''A second answer finds its operation already closed by the first answer, and fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_16a
          desc: '''The RMW filter shall send the meta SRAM at most one `Get` of the meta word per accepted request.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_single_op"
          checks: ["nothing else downstream (assert_RmwSingleOp_NothingElseDownstream)"]
          why: '''The check allows one `Get` for each request. A second `Get`, or one with no request, fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_16b
          desc: '''The RMW filter shall send the meta SRAM a `PutFullData` write-back only for a write whose tag differs from the stored bit, and at most one per write.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_single_op"
          checks: ["nothing else downstream (assert_RmwSingleOp_NothingElseDownstream)"]
          why: '''A write-back is allowed once, and only for the current write whose bit differs. A write-back for a read, for an equal bit, or a second one fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_17
          desc: '''`d_error` upstream shall be clear when neither the `Get` answer nor the write-back answer of the operation has a device error.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_errors"
          checks: ["no error without a cause (assert_RmwErrors_NoErrorWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''An answer with `d_error` whose `Get` and write-back answers had none fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_RMW_18
          desc: '''Every `Get` the RMW filter generates shall carry a valid command integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Description](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/README.md#description)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `BUS.INTEGRITY`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rmw_read"
          checks: ["Get carries valid integrity (assert_RmwRead_GetCarriesValidIntegrity)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the command integrity of every `Get`, for reads and writes. No other check covers it, because the TL-UL ABVIP checks no integrity field.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Tag path alerts'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state when the tag path raises the fatal alert `fatal_fault`.'''
        '''The Registers and alert group says what raising the alert means on `alert_tx_o`.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_07
          desc: '''A device error on the tag path shall raise `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_alerts"
          checks: ["device error raises alert (assert_TagAlerts_DeviceErrorRaisesAlert)"]
          why: '''The formal tool searches for a run in which a meta SRAM answer with `d_error` never raises the alert request. No specification states how soon the alert follows, so the check has no time bound. It needs no assumption about the neighbours, because none of them can hold the alert back.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_08
          desc: '''An integrity fault on a meta SRAM response to the tag path shall raise `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_alerts"
          checks: ["integrity fault raises alert (assert_TagAlerts_IntegrityFaultRaisesAlert)"]
          why: '''The formal tool searches for a run in which a meta SRAM answer with a broken integrity, with or without `d_error`, never raises the alert request. No specification states how soon the alert follows, so the check has no time bound. It needs no assumption about the neighbours, because none of them can hold the alert back.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_12
          desc: '''A core request whose tag sideband holds an invalid encoding shall raise `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `CORED_TAG.INTERSIG.MUBI`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_alerts"
          checks: ["invalid request tag raises alert (assert_TagAlerts_InvalidRequestTagRaisesAlert)"]
          why: '''The formal tool searches for a run in which a core request with an invalid tag sideband, a read or a write in either mode, never raises the alert request. No specification states how soon the alert follows. A design that decodes the sideband without checking its encoding never raises the alert and fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_10
          desc: '''Outside the alert handler's in-band reset, once `fatal_fault` is raised, the subsystem shall send alert events on `alert_tx_o` repeatedly until reset, whatever raised it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
            '''[Alerts per Module](doc/contributing/hw/comportability/README.md#alerts-per-module)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["fatal alert repeats (assert_Alert_FatalAlertRepeats)", "failed request alerts (assert_Alert_FailedRequestAlerts)", "fault input alerts (assert_Alert_FaultInputAlerts)"]
          why: '''From the first failed request or fault input on, the check requires an alert event within `AlertLat` cycles of every cycle until reset. A sender that sends one event and stops fails the check. The fault inputs are free here, so the check holds whatever raised them.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Access checkers'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state which requests from the four requester ports reach `meta_sram_tl`, and how the subsystem answers a request that is not legal.'''
        '''Each row is checked at those ports and at `meta_sram_tl`, with the 4:1 arbiter in place.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_META_01a
          desc: '''A legal request on a requester port shall be forwarded to `meta_sram_tl`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''The check requires every legal request that a requester port presents to appear on `meta_sram_tl`. A legal request that is dropped, or refused with an error answer, never appears there and fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_01b
          desc: '''A legal request on a requester port shall be forwarded to `meta_sram_tl` at most once.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["no extra meta SRAM request (assert_MetaForward_NoExtraMetaSramRequest)"]
          why: '''The check requires each request on `meta_sram_tl` to match a legal request that is not yet forwarded. A second copy of a request finds that request already forwarded, so it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_03
          desc: '''No request outside its port's region shall reach `meta_sram_tl`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `ACCESS_CHECK`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `MEM.SW_NOACCESS`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["in own region (assert_MetaRefuse_InOwnRegion)"]
          why: '''The check finds the requester port from the source ID that the request carries on `meta_sram_tl`, and compares the address with the region of that port. The check fails when a port that owns the bitmap reaches a tag word, or when the tag port reaches the bitmap.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_04
          desc: '''Outside CHERIoT mode, no request from any requester port shall reach `meta_sram_tl`. This holds for every value of `cheriot_ena_i` other than `MuBi4True`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `MODE_GATING`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `INTERSIG.MUBI`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["only in CHERIoT mode (assert_MetaRefuse_OnlyInCHERIoTMode)"]
          why: '''The check fails on any request on `meta_sram_tl` while the mode enable is not `MuBi4True`. The check covers a strict `MuBi4False` and every invalid encoding.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_05
          desc: '''No request that is not a full 32-bit word at a word-aligned address shall reach `meta_sram_tl`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["only full words (assert_MetaRefuse_OnlyFullWords)"]
          why: '''The check fails on any request on `meta_sram_tl` that is not a full word at a word-aligned address. A forwarded one- or two-byte `Get` fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_06
          desc: '''No request whose opcode is not `Get` or `PutFullData` shall reach `meta_sram_tl`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["only Get or PutFullData (assert_MetaRefuse_OnlyGetOrPutFullData)"]
          why: '''The check fails on any request on `meta_sram_tl` whose opcode is not `Get` or `PutFullData`. A forwarded `PutPartialData` fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_07a
          desc: '''A request that is not legal shall be answered.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["request eventually answered (assert_MetaFlow_RequestEventuallyAnswered)"]
          why: '''The check covers every accepted request, including a request that is not legal. The formal tool searches for a run in which a request that is not legal is never answered. Such a run fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_07b
          desc: '''A request that is not legal shall be answered at most once.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["no extra answer (assert_MetaFlow_NoExtraAnswer)"]
          why: '''The check requires each answer to name a request that is outstanding on its port. This rule is one of the TL-UL rules on each requester port. A second error answer to one request names no outstanding request, so it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_07c
          desc: '''The answer to a request that is not legal shall have `d_error` set.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["illegal request gets error (assert_MetaRefuse_IllegalRequestGetsError)"]
          why: '''The check looks at the answer to every request that is not legal. An answer with `d_error` at 0 fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_16a
          desc: '''An access checker's error answer shall carry a valid response integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
            '''[Description](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/README.md#description)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["error answer carries valid integrity (assert_MetaRefuse_ErrorAnswerCarriesValidIntegrity)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the response integrity of every error answer. An error answer with a broken response integrity fails the check. A refusal that software can cause must not become an integrity fault at the requester.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_16b
          desc: '''An access checker's error answer to a `Get` shall carry a valid data integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
            '''[Description](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/README.md#description)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_refuse"
          checks: ["error answer carries valid integrity (assert_MetaRefuse_ErrorAnswerCarriesValidIntegrity)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the data integrity of the error answer to every `Get` that is not legal. An error answer with a broken data integrity fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''4:1 arbiter'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state how the 4:1 arbiter (`tlul_socket_m1`) carries requests to `meta_sram_tl` and answers back to the four requester ports.'''
        '''Each row is checked at those ports, with the access checkers in place.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_META_02a
          desc: '''A request forwarded to `meta_sram_tl` shall carry the opcode (`a_opcode`) of the original request on its requester port, unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded `a_opcode` with the requester's `a_opcode`. A `Get` turned into a `PutFullData`, or the reverse, fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_02b
          desc: '''A request forwarded to `meta_sram_tl` shall carry the param (`a_param`) of the original request on its requester port, unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded `a_param` with the requester's `a_param`. Any changed bit fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_02c
          desc: '''A request forwarded to `meta_sram_tl` shall carry the address (`a_address`) of the original request on its requester port, unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded `a_address` with the requester's `a_address`. Any changed bit fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_02d
          desc: '''A request forwarded to `meta_sram_tl` shall carry the data (`a_data`) of the original request on its requester port, unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded `a_data` with the requester's `a_data`. Any changed data bit of a write fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_02e
          desc: '''A request forwarded to `meta_sram_tl` shall carry the size (`a_size`) of the original request on its requester port, unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded `a_size` with the requester's `a_size`. A changed size fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_02f
          desc: '''A request forwarded to `meta_sram_tl` shall carry the byte mask (`a_mask`) of the original request on its requester port, unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded `a_mask` with the requester's `a_mask`. A byte added to the mask or dropped from it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_02g
          desc: '''A request forwarded to `meta_sram_tl` shall carry the user bits (`a_user`, with its command and data integrity) of the original request on its requester port, unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''The check compares the forwarded `a_user` with the requester's `a_user`. The comparison includes the command integrity and the data integrity that `a_user` carries. Any changed bit fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_08
          desc: '''No request shall reach `meta_sram_tl` that no requester port presented.'''
          source: [
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["no extra meta SRAM request (assert_MetaForward_NoExtraMetaSramRequest)"]
          why: '''A request on `meta_sram_tl` for which no requester port presented a legal request matches nothing, so it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_09a
          desc: '''Every answer from `meta_sram_tl` shall reach the requester port whose request it answers.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID growth](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-growth)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["answer to its port (assert_MetaReturn_AnswerToItsPort)", "taken with its port (assert_MetaReturn_TakenWithItsPort)"]
          why: '''The first check requires the answer to appear at the requester port that its source ID names. The second check requires that the meta SRAM's answer is taken only when that port takes it. A dropped answer, or an answer taken before its port takes it, fails one of the two checks.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_09b
          desc: '''No answer from `meta_sram_tl` shall reach a requester port other than the one whose request it answers.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID growth](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-growth)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["only the meta SRAM's answer (assert_MetaReturn_OnlyTheMetaSRAMsAnswer)"]
          why: '''The check requires that, in each cycle in which a port receives an answer, the meta SRAM sends an answer to that port. An answer copied to a second port, or sent to the wrong port, has no such answer from the meta SRAM, so it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_10
          desc: '''An answer shall carry, as its `d_source`, the `a_source` that its requester sent with the request.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["source shifted back (assert_MetaReturn_SourceShiftedBack)"]
          why: '''The check compares the answer's `d_source` with the meta SRAM's `d_source` shifted right by two. When the meta SRAM returns the source ID that the request carried on `meta_sram_tl`, the shifted value is the requester's own `a_source`. A wrong shift fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_11a
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its requester with its opcode (`d_opcode`) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_MetaReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares the answer's `d_opcode` with the meta SRAM's `d_opcode`. A changed opcode fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_11b
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its requester with its error (`d_error`) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_MetaReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares the answer's `d_error` with the meta SRAM's `d_error`. An error that is dropped or added fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_11c
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its requester with its param (`d_param`) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_MetaReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares the answer's `d_param` with the meta SRAM's `d_param`. Any changed bit fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_11d
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its requester with its size (`d_size`) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_MetaReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares the answer's `d_size` with the meta SRAM's `d_size`. A changed size fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_11e
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its requester with its data (`d_data`) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_MetaReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares the `d_data` of every `AccessAckData` with the meta SRAM's `d_data`. Any changed data bit fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_11f
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its requester with its sink ID (`d_sink`) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_MetaReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares the answer's `d_sink` with the meta SRAM's `d_sink`. A changed sink ID fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_11g
          desc: '''An answer shall reach its requester with its user bits (`d_user`, with its response and data integrity) unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
            '''[Arbitration](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#arbitration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["fields unchanged (assert_MetaReturn_FieldsUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares the answer's `d_user` with the meta SRAM's `d_user`. The comparison includes the response integrity and the data integrity that `d_user` carries. Any changed bit fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_12
          desc: '''A request held on a requester port shall eventually be accepted, provided that the meta SRAM keeps accepting requests.'''
          source: [
            '''[`tlul_socket_m1`](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#tlul_socket_m1)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_flow"
          checks: ["round robin bound (assert_MetaFlow_RoundRobinBound)", "request eventually accepted (assert_MetaFlow_RequestEventuallyAccepted)"]
          why: '''While a request waits at the 4:1 arbiter, the first check requires that the arbiter forward at most three requests of other ports before it. The request is therefore forwarded while the meta SRAM keeps accepting. At the requester port, a run in which a held request waits forever while the meta SRAM keeps accepting fails the second check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_13a
          desc: '''Every accepted request shall be answered, provided that the meta SRAM answers and every requester takes its answers.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_flow"
          checks: ["request eventually answered (assert_MetaFlow_RequestEventuallyAnswered)"]
          why: '''The formal tool searches for a run in which an accepted request is never answered, while the meta SRAM answers and the requesters take their answers. Such a run fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_13b
          desc: '''Every accepted request shall be answered at most once.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_flow"
          checks: ["no extra answer (assert_MetaFlow_NoExtraAnswer)"]
          why: '''The check requires each answer to name a request that is outstanding on its port. A second answer to one request names no outstanding request, so it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_14
          desc: '''A legal request that is presented while no other requester port presents a request shall reach `meta_sram_tl` in the same cycle.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_forward"
          checks: ["legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)"]
          why: '''While no other port presents a request, the check requires a legal request to appear on `meta_sram_tl` in the same cycle in which it is presented. A request that appears one cycle late fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_META_15
          desc: '''An answer from `meta_sram_tl` shall reach its requester in the cycle in which it arrives.'''
          source: [
            '''[Timing](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#timing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "meta_return"
          checks: ["answer to its port (assert_MetaReturn_AnswerToItsPort)"]
          why: '''The check requires the answer to appear at its port in the same cycle in which it arrives on `meta_sram_tl`. An answer that reaches its port one cycle late fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V1"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Tag store isolation'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state which part of the meta SRAM each requester port reaches: the tag port reaches only the capability tag regions, and no other port reaches them.'''
        '''The rows apply the access rules to the tag port.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_05
          desc: '''Tag path accesses shall reach only the capability tag regions of the meta SRAM.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[Meta SRAM Address Map](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#meta-sram-address-map)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_isolation"
          checks: ["tag port in tag regions (assert_TagIsolation_TagPortInTagRegions)"]
          why: '''The check finds the requester port from the source ID that the request carries on `meta_sram_tl`. The check fails on a request from the tag port outside `0x1100_0C00`-`0x1100_97FF`. A request from the tag port that reaches the bitmap fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_06
          desc: '''Outside CHERIoT mode, no tag path access shall reach the meta SRAM.'''
          source: [
            '''[Access Checkers](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#access-checkers)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `INTERSIG.MUBI`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_isolation"
          checks: ["tag port only in CHERIoT mode (assert_TagIsolation_TagPortOnlyInCHERIoTMode)"]
          why: '''The check fails on any request from the tag port on `meta_sram_tl` while the mode enable is not `MuBi4True`. The check covers each of the 16 values of the mode enable.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_11
          desc: '''No meta SRAM request from a requester port other than the tag port shall reach a capability tag region.'''
          source: [
            '''[Meta SRAM Address Map](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#meta-sram-address-map)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_isolation"
          checks: ["other ports never reach tags (assert_TagIsolation_OtherPortsNeverReachTags)"]
          why: '''The check fails on any request inside `0x1100_0C00`-`0x1100_97FF` from one of the three requester ports other than the tag port. A software read of a tag word through `revbm_tl_d` fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Start, status and interrupt'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state which starts the engine takes, the status of a sweep in `TBRE_REGWEN`, `TBRE_STATUS` and `TBRE_EPOCH`, and the `tbre_done` interrupt.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_01
          desc: '''A taken start shall start a sweep over the swept capabilities.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TBRE_SWEEP`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_start"
          checks: ["taken start activates (assert_TbreStart_TakenStartActivates)", "REGWEN falls only on start (assert_TbreStart_RegwenFallsOnlyOnStart)"]
          why: '''The first check requires the engine to be active in the cycle after every taken start. The second check allows the engine to become active only in the cycle after a taken start. A design that drops a taken start keeps `TBRE_REGWEN` at 1 and fails the first check. The checks of `tbre_sweep` decide which words the sweep reads.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_02a
          desc: '''An ignored start shall start no sweep.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_start"
          checks: ["REGWEN falls only on start (assert_TbreStart_RegwenFallsOnlyOnStart)"]
          why: '''The check allows `TBRE_REGWEN` to fall only in the cycle after a taken start. A sweep started by an ignored start makes `TBRE_REGWEN` fall with no taken start before it, so it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_02b
          desc: '''An ignored start shall leave `TBRE_STATUS.busy` unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_start"
          checks: ["ignored start changes nothing (assert_TbreStart_IgnoredStartChangesNothing)"]
          why: '''An ignored start comes only while the engine is idle. The check requires the value that the engine last wrote into `TBRE_STATUS.busy` to be 0 in the cycle after an ignored start. A busy value that the start raises fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_02c
          desc: '''An ignored start shall leave `TBRE_REGWEN` unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_start"
          checks: ["ignored start changes nothing (assert_TbreStart_IgnoredStartChangesNothing)"]
          why: '''The check requires `TBRE_REGWEN` to still be 1 in the cycle after an ignored start. A fall of `TBRE_REGWEN` fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_02d
          desc: '''An ignored start shall leave `TBRE_EPOCH` unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_start"
          checks: ["ignored start changes nothing (assert_TbreStart_IgnoredStartChangesNothing)"]
          why: '''The check compares `TBRE_EPOCH` in the cycle after an ignored start with its value before the start. Any change fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_03
          desc: '''An ignored start shall set `TBRE_STATUS.start_err`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Revoking Capabilities](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#revoking-capabilities)'''
            '''No specification states how soon the error is set.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_start"
          checks: ["ignored start sets error (assert_TbreStart_IgnoredStartSetsError)", "error set next cycle (assert_TbreStart_ErrorSetNextCycle)"]
          why: '''The first check requires a request to set `start_err` after every ignored start. The second check requires that request by the next cycle, so the first read after the start returns `start_err` set. The check takes the next cycle. A design that skips or delays the request fails one of the two checks.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_04a
          desc: '''Only an ignored start shall set `TBRE_STATUS.start_err`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Errors](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#errors)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_start"
          checks: ["error only after ignored start (assert_TbreStart_ErrorOnlyAfterIgnoredStart)"]
          why: '''The check allows a request to set `start_err` only while an ignored start has not yet had one. A request after a taken start, or a second request for one ignored start, fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_04b
          desc: '''`TBRE_STATUS.start_err` shall stay set until software writes 1 to it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''!!TBRE_STATUS.start_err'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The mirror takes the hardware's writes on `hw2reg` and clears the bit only on a software write of 1. A bit that the register file clears on its own fails the comparison. The check does not show that the engine never writes 0 to it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_05a
          desc: '''While `TBRE_REGWEN` is 0, a write to `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` shall have no effect.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_REGWEN.en'''
            '''[Revoking Capabilities](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#revoking-capabilities)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["locked base stable (assert_Csr_LockedBaseStable)", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''Any change of `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` in the cycle after a cycle in which `TBRE_REGWEN` is 0 fails the check, whatever causes the change.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_05b
          desc: '''While `TBRE_REGWEN` is 0, a write to `TBRE_NUM_CAPS` shall have no effect.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_REGWEN.en'''
            '''[Revoking Capabilities](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#revoking-capabilities)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["locked num stable (assert_Csr_LockedNumStable)", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''Any change of `TBRE_NUM_CAPS` in the cycle after a cycle in which `TBRE_REGWEN` is 0 fails the check, whatever causes the change.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_05c
          desc: '''While `TBRE_REGWEN` is 0, a write to `TBRE_START` shall have no effect.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_REGWEN.en'''
            '''[Revoking Capabilities](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#revoking-capabilities)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["locked start no strobe (assert_Csr_LockedStartNoStrobe)", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The check fails when a write to `TBRE_START` while `TBRE_REGWEN` is 0 produces a start strobe in its own cycle or in the next cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_06a
          desc: '''Bits 31:3 of `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` shall keep the value that software wrote.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_BASE_ADDR'''
            '''!!TBRE_BASE_ADDR.addr'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["base written (assert_Csr_BaseWritten)", "base changes only by write (assert_Csr_BaseChangesOnlyByWrite)", "read returns register (assert_Csr_ReadReturnsRegister)"]
          why: '''The checks require that a write to `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` takes effect, that nothing else changes the register, and that a read returns its value. A value that is lost, changed or misread therefore fails one of them.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_06b
          desc: '''`TBRE_NUM_CAPS` shall keep the value that software wrote.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_NUM_CAPS.num'''
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["num written (assert_Csr_NumWritten)", "num changes only by write (assert_Csr_NumChangesOnlyByWrite)", "read returns register (assert_Csr_ReadReturnsRegister)"]
          why: '''The checks require that a write to `TBRE_NUM_CAPS` takes effect, that nothing else changes the register, and that a read returns its value. A value that is lost, changed or misread therefore fails one of them.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_06c
          desc: '''Bits 2:0 of `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` shall read as zero.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_BASE_ADDR.addr'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["read returns register (assert_Csr_ReadReturnsRegister)"]
          why: '''A read of `TBRE_BASE_ADDR` that returns any of bits 2:0 set fails the check. The check covers every read of a whole, aligned word with valid command and data integrity.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_07a
          desc: '''`TBRE_REGWEN` shall be 0 from the cycle after a taken start until every swept capability of that sweep is resolved.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''No specification states when a capability counts as resolved.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_status"
          checks: ["REGWEN low after start (assert_TbreStatus_RegwenLowAfterStart)", "REGWEN rises only when resolved (assert_TbreStatus_RegwenRisesOnlyWhenResolved)"]
          why: '''The first check requires `TBRE_REGWEN` to fall in the cycle after the start. The tracked capability of the second check can be any swept capability. A rise of `TBRE_REGWEN` while that capability is not yet resolved fails the second check. A rise of `TBRE_REGWEN` while a read, a lookup or a clear of the engine is outstanding fails it too.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_07b
          desc: '''`TBRE_REGWEN` shall be 1 in every cycle, except from the cycle after a taken start until every swept capability of that sweep is resolved.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_status"
          checks: ["REGWEN falls only on start (assert_TbreStart_RegwenFallsOnlyOnStart)"]
          why: '''Outside a sweep, the check allows `TBRE_REGWEN` to fall only in the cycle after a taken start. `TBRE_REGWEN` therefore stays 1 until a sweep starts. No check requires the rise at the moment every swept capability is resolved, because no specification states when a capability counts as resolved. The check *sweep ends* of `tbre_done` only requires the rise at some point.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_08
          desc: '''`TBRE_STATUS.busy` shall equal the inverse of the value that `TBRE_REGWEN` had one cycle earlier.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''!!TBRE_REGWEN.en'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_status"
          checks: ["busy follows REGWEN (assert_TbreStatus_BusyFollowsRegwen)"]
          why: '''In every cycle, the check compares the value that the engine last wrote into `TBRE_STATUS.busy` with the inverse of `TBRE_REGWEN` in the cycle before. A busy value that changes too early or too late, or that is stuck, fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_09
          desc: '''`TBRE_EPOCH.active` shall equal the inverse of `TBRE_REGWEN` in every cycle.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_EPOCH.active'''
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_status"
          checks: ["active follows REGWEN (assert_TbreStatus_ActiveFollowsRegwen)"]
          why: '''In every cycle, the check compares `TBRE_EPOCH.active` with the inverse of `TBRE_REGWEN`. An active bit that is one cycle early or late fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_10
          desc: '''`TBRE_EPOCH.count` shall increase by one, modulo 2^31, in the cycle in which `TBRE_EPOCH.active` clears, if no error set `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err` during that sweep.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''!!TBRE_EPOCH.count'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_epoch"
          checks: ["steps unless error (assert_TbreEpoch_StepsUnlessError)"]
          why: '''The check computes the expected count from the old count and from the error causes seen in the sweep. A missed step, a step of 2 or a wrong wrap fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_11
          desc: '''`TBRE_EPOCH.count` shall change only in a cycle in which `TBRE_EPOCH.active` clears at the end of a sweep, and only if no error set `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err` during that sweep.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_epoch"
          checks: ["steps unless error (assert_TbreEpoch_StepsUnlessError)", "count stable otherwise (assert_TbreEpoch_CountStableOtherwise)"]
          why: '''A step of the count at the end of a sweep with an error fails the first check. A change of the count in any other cycle fails the second check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_12a
          desc: '''The first register read that the register interface accepts after the write of a taken start shall return `TBRE_REGWEN` = 0.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Tracking Completed Sweeps](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#tracking-completed-sweeps)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_status"
          checks: ["REGWEN low after start (assert_TbreStatus_RegwenLowAfterStart)"]
          why: '''The check requires `TBRE_REGWEN` to be 0 from the cycle after the start. The register interface accepts a request at most every other cycle, so the first read that it accepts after the start cannot come before that cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_12b
          desc: '''The first register read that the register interface accepts after the write of a taken start shall return `TBRE_EPOCH.active` = 1.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tracking Completed Sweeps](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#tracking-completed-sweeps)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_status"
          checks: ["REGWEN low after start (assert_TbreStatus_RegwenLowAfterStart)", "active follows REGWEN (assert_TbreStatus_ActiveFollowsRegwen)"]
          why: '''The two checks require `TBRE_EPOCH.active` to be 1 from the cycle after the start. The register interface accepts a request at most every other cycle, so the first read after the start cannot come before that cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_12c
          desc: '''The first register read that the register interface accepts after the write of a taken start shall return `TBRE_STATUS.busy` = 1.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Tracking Completed Sweeps](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#tracking-completed-sweeps)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_status"
          checks: ["REGWEN low after start (assert_TbreStatus_RegwenLowAfterStart)", "busy follows REGWEN (assert_TbreStatus_BusyFollowsRegwen)"]
          why: '''The two checks require the value that the engine last wrote into `TBRE_STATUS.busy` to be 1 two cycles after the start write. The register interface accepts a request at most every other cycle, so it accepts no read before then.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_28
          desc: '''`INTR_STATE.tbre_done` shall be set when the engine stops being active, and when software writes 1 to `INTR_TEST.tbre_done`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Interrupts](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/interfaces.md#interrupts)'''
            '''!!INTR_TEST'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_intr"
          checks: ["sweep end or test sets (assert_TbreIntr_SweepEndOrTestSets)"]
          why: '''The check requires a request to set `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` in the cycle in which `TBRE_REGWEN` rises. It also requires one in the cycle of a test write, which is a write of 1 to `INTR_TEST.tbre_done`. A sweep end or a test write with no such request fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_29a
          desc: '''`INTR_STATE.tbre_done` shall stay set until software writes 1 to it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tracking Completed Sweeps](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#tracking-completed-sweeps)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["intr stays set (assert_Csr_IntrStaysSet)"]
          why: '''A clear of `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` without a software write of 1 fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_29b
          desc: '''A software write of 1 to `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` in the cycle in which a sweep ends shall leave `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` clear.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tracking Completed Sweeps](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#tracking-completed-sweeps)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["intr clear wins (assert_Csr_IntrClearWins)"]
          why: '''The check fails when software writes 1 to `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` in the cycle of a set request for that bit, and the bit is set afterwards.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_30
          desc: '''`INTR_STATE.tbre_done` shall be set only when the engine stops being active or when software writes 1 to `INTR_TEST.tbre_done`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Interrupts](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/interfaces.md#interrupts)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_intr"
          checks: ["set only on end or test (assert_TbreIntr_SetOnlyOnEndOrTest)"]
          why: '''A request to set `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` in a cycle with no sweep end and no write of 1 to `INTR_TEST.tbre_done` fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_31
          desc: '''`intr_tbre_done_o` shall be high exactly when `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` and `INTR_ENABLE.tbre_done` are both set, after one fixed latency of at most one cycle, so that no one-cycle pulse is lost.'''
          source: [
            '''[Register Creation](doc/contributing/hw/comportability/README.md#register-creation)'''
            '''[Event Type Interrupt](doc/contributing/hw/comportability/README.md#event-type-interrupt)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_intr"
          checks: ["line follows state (assert_TbreIntr_LineFollowsState)"]
          why: '''The check computes whether `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` and `INTR_ENABLE.tbre_done` were both set one fixed latency earlier. In every cycle, the check compares `intr_tbre_done_o` with that result. A line that misses a one-cycle pulse, or that stays high after the two fields stopped being both set, fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Sweep'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state which reads the engine makes on `tbre_tl_h`, and how every sweep ends.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_13
          desc: '''A sweep shall read both words of every swept capability on `tbre_tl_h`, each with a full-word `Get`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TBRE_SWEEP`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_sweep"
          checks: ["both words read (assert_TbreSweep_BothWordsRead)"]
          why: '''The formal tool may choose any swept capability as the tracked one. The check requires an accepted full-word `Get` of each word of the tracked capability before the sweep ends. A skipped word fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_14
          desc: '''`tbre_tl_h` shall carry only full-word `Get` requests, each for a word of a swept capability of the sweep in progress.'''
          source: [
            '''[Block Diagram](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#block-diagram)'''
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_sweep"
          checks: ["Gets inside sweep (assert_TbreSweep_GetsInsideSweep)"]
          why: '''The check compares every request on `tbre_tl_h` with the range, the opcode and the size that the sweep allows. A write, a sub-word read, a read outside the range or a read while the engine is idle fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_15a
          desc: '''At most two reads shall be outstanding on `tbre_tl_h`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_sweep"
          checks: ["at most two outstanding (assert_TbreSweep_AtMostTwoOutstanding)"]
          why: '''The check counts the reads accepted on `tbre_tl_h` and not yet answered. A third outstanding read fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_15b
          desc: '''Each outstanding read on `tbre_tl_h` shall carry an `a_source` that no other outstanding read uses.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_sweep"
          checks: ["at most two outstanding (assert_TbreSweep_AtMostTwoOutstanding)"]
          why: '''The TL-UL ABVIP fails a read that uses the `a_source` of a read that is still outstanding.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_16
          desc: '''The engine shall read every word with the capability-load hint.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_sweep"
          checks: ["Gets carry hint (assert_TbreSweep_GetsCarryHint)"]
          why: '''The check looks at every `Get` that reaches the engine's tag filter. A `Get` without the capability-load hint fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_37
          desc: '''Every sweep shall end, provided that `xbar_main`, the engine's bitmap port and the RMW filter answer the engine's requests.'''
          source: [
            '''[Interrupts](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/interfaces.md#interrupts)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_done"
          checks: ["sweep ends (assert_TbreDone_SweepEnds)"]
          why: '''The formal tool looks for a run in which the neighbours of the engine answer and `TBRE_REGWEN` stays 0 forever. A sweep that hangs gives such a run, so it fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_40
          desc: '''Every read that the engine generates on `tbre_tl_h` shall carry a valid command integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Description](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/README.md#description)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `BUS.INTEGRITY`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_sweep"
          checks: ["sweep read carries valid integrity (assert_TbreSweep_SweepReadCarriesValidIntegrity)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the command integrity of every read presented on `tbre_tl_h`. No other check covers the integrity, because the TL-UL ABVIP leaves every integrity field free.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Decision and clears'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state the bitmap lookup, which swept capabilities are revoked, and the clear through the engine's tag filter.'''
        '''The End-to-end requirements group holds the result of a whole sweep: a revoked capability reads back untagged, and a capability that the core wrote keeps its tag.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_17
          desc: '''For every swept capability that is tagged, is not a sealing capability and has its base in the main SRAM region, the engine shall look up the bitmap word that holds the revocation bit of its base, with a full-word `Get` on its bitmap port.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Meta SRAM Address Map](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#meta-sram-address-map)'''
            '''No specification states when the lookup happens.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_decision"
          checks: ["lookup when needed (assert_TbreDecision_LookupWhenNeeded)", "lookup is bitmap Get (assert_TbreDecision_LookupIsBitmapGet)"]
          why: '''For a tracked capability that needs a lookup, the first check requires a full-word `Get` of the bitmap word of its base within a defined time (the check takes the time in which the TRVK filter holds the capability's W1 answer). A lookup outside the bitmap, or a second lookup for one W1 answer, fails the second check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_18
          desc: '''The engine shall make no bitmap lookup for a capability whose base lies outside the main SRAM region.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revoking Capabilities](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#revoking-capabilities)'''
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_decision"
          checks: ["no lookup outside main SRAM (assert_TbreDecision_NoLookupOutsideMainSram)", "lookup is bitmap Get (assert_TbreDecision_LookupIsBitmapGet)"]
          why: '''The first check looks at the time in which the TRVK filter holds the W1 answer of a capability whose base lies outside the main SRAM region. A lookup in that time fails the first check. The second check ties every lookup to a W1 answer, so no lookup falls outside that time.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_19
          desc: '''The engine shall present a clear for every revoked swept capability whose reads were answered without error and that no core write touched in its watch window.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TBRE_SWEEP`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_decision"
          checks: ["revoked gets cleared (assert_TbreDecision_RevokedGetsCleared)"]
          why: '''From the decoded base, the permissions and the bitmap word of the capability, the check decides whether the capability is revoked. The check requires the clear before the sweep ends. A revoked capability that is left tagged fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_20
          desc: '''The engine shall present no clear for a tagged swept capability that is not revoked.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Revoking Capabilities](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#revoking-capabilities)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_decision"
          checks: ["clear only if revoked (assert_TbreDecision_ClearOnlyIfRevoked)"]
          why: '''The check requires every clear to belong to a swept capability that is revoked. A clear fails the check when its capability is a sealing capability, when its base lies outside the main SRAM region, or when the revocation bit of its base is clear.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_21a
          desc: '''A clear shall be one tag write that writes tag 0.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["clears tracked bit once (assert_TbreClear_ClearsTrackedBitOnce)", "writes tag 0 (assert_TbreClear_WritesTag0)"]
          why: '''The first check requires the clear of the tracked capability to be one write of tag 0. Any write from the engine's tag filter that carries tag 1 fails the second check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_21b
          desc: '''A clear shall address the meta word that holds the capability's tag bit.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''No specification states the bit order of the tags within a meta word.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["clears tracked bit once (assert_TbreClear_ClearsTrackedBitOnce)"]
          why: '''The check compares the address of the clear with the meta word that holds the tag bit of the tracked capability. A clear to another word fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_21c
          desc: '''The bit select of a clear shall name the tag bit of the capability within the meta word.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
            '''No specification states the bit order of the tags within a meta word.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["clears tracked bit once (assert_TbreClear_ClearsTrackedBitOnce)"]
          why: '''The check compares the bit select of the clear with the tag bit of the tracked capability. A clear to another bit fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_21d
          desc: '''A clear shall be presented on the input of the 2:1 tag arbiter that comes from the engine's tag filter.'''
          source: [
            '''[RMW Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#rmw-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["clears tracked bit once (assert_TbreClear_ClearsTrackedBitOnce)"]
          why: '''The check looks for the clear only on the input of the 2:1 tag arbiter that comes from the engine's tag filter. A clear on any other port fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_21e
          desc: '''The engine shall present at most one clear per capability per sweep.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["clears tracked bit once (assert_TbreClear_ClearsTrackedBitOnce)"]
          why: '''After the clear of the tracked capability, a second clear of the same capability in the same sweep fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_22
          desc: '''The engine's tag filter shall meet the tag filter requirements (`REQ_TF_*`) for reads on its own device, host and meta ports.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["tag filter checks hold (assert_TbreClear_TagFilterChecksHold)"]
          why: '''The checks of the tag filter testpoints also apply to the ports of the engine's tag filter. A read that breaks a tag filter rule there fails the same check that it would fail on the core's tag filter.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_23a
          desc: '''A write to the engine's tag filter shall issue one meta request, which is the tag write.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["write answered once (assert_TbreClear_WriteAnsweredOnce)"]
          why: '''The check counts the meta requests that each write to the engine's tag filter makes. A write with no meta request, or a write with two meta requests, fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_23b
          desc: '''A write to the engine's tag filter shall issue no request on `tbre_tl_h`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["write answered once (assert_TbreClear_WriteAnsweredOnce)"]
          why: '''Any request on `tbre_tl_h` that a write to the engine's tag filter causes fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_23c
          desc: '''A write to the engine's tag filter shall be answered once.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["write answered once (assert_TbreClear_WriteAnsweredOnce)"]
          why: '''The check counts the answers to each write to the engine's tag filter. A lost answer, or a second answer, fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_23d
          desc: '''The answer to a write to the engine's tag filter shall carry the error of its tag write.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "tbre_clear"
          checks: ["write answered once (assert_TbreClear_WriteAnsweredOnce)"]
          why: '''The check compares the `d_error` of the answer to a write with the `d_error` of the answer to its meta request. An error that is dropped or invented fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_41
          desc: '''Every bitmap lookup that the engine generates shall carry a valid command integrity.'''
          source: [
            '''[Description](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/README.md#description)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `BUS.INTEGRITY`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_decision"
          checks: ["lookup carries valid integrity (assert_TbreDecision_LookupCarriesValidIntegrity)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the command integrity of every lookup presented. No other check covers the integrity, because the TL-UL ABVIP leaves every integrity field free.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Core write watch'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state which core writes the subsystem watches during a sweep.'''
        '''They also state how the tag clear squash works: a clear for a capability that the core wrote is never presented, or it reaches the RMW filter as a read.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_24
          desc: '''The engine shall present no clear for a capability that a core write touched in its watch window.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TBRE_CORE_WRITE_SNOOP`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_watch"
          checks: ["clear only if untouched (assert_TbreWatch_ClearOnlyIfUntouched)"]
          why: '''The check records every touch of the tracked capability from the read of its W0 onwards. A clear that is presented after a touch fails the check. The window starts and ends at the engine's own read and clear ports.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_25
          desc: '''A clear for a capability that a core write touches between the presentation of the clear and its arrival at the RMW filter shall reach the RMW filter as a read of the tag word, not as a write.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_watch"
          checks: ["stale clear becomes read (assert_TbreWatch_StaleClearBecomesRead)"]
          why: '''A core write may touch the capability between the presentation of its clear and the arrival of the clear at the RMW filter. For such a clear, the check requires a `Get` of the same word and bit at the RMW filter. A clear that still arrives as a write fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_26
          desc: '''A clear that no core write touches between the presentation of the clear and its arrival at the RMW filter shall reach the RMW filter as a write of tag 0.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_watch"
          checks: ["fresh clear stays write (assert_TbreWatch_FreshClearStaysWrite)"]
          why: '''The check compares the request at the RMW filter with the request that the 2:1 tag arbiter forwards. A clear that becomes a read with no touch fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_27a
          desc: '''Once a clear is presented at the RMW filter, it shall stay presented until the RMW filter accepts it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_watch"
          checks: ["clear held unchanged (assert_TbreWatch_ClearHeldUnchanged)"]
          why: '''A clear that is withdrawn before it is accepted, or that a core write displaces, fails the check in the next cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_27b
          desc: '''Once a clear is presented at the RMW filter, it shall stay unchanged until the RMW filter accepts it.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_watch"
          checks: ["clear held unchanged (assert_TbreWatch_ClearHeldUnchanged)"]
          why: '''The check compares every field of a clear that waits at the RMW filter with its value in the cycle before. A changed field fails the check. A clear that is turned into a read after it arrived also fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Sweep errors'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state which errors fail a sweep, by setting `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err`, and which of them raise `fatal_fault`.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_32a
          desc: '''When a sweep read is answered with `d_error`, the engine shall present no clear for the capability of that read.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["read error, no clear (assert_TbreErrors_ReadErrorNoClear)"]
          why: '''The formal tool may choose any capability as the tracked one. A clear for the tracked capability after a `d_error` on one of its reads fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_32b
          desc: '''A sweep read answered with `d_error` shall set `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
            '''No specification states how soon the error is set.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["cause sets sweep error (assert_TbreErrors_CauseSetsSweepError)", "error set next cycle (assert_TbreErrors_ErrorSetNextCycle)"]
          why: '''The first check requires a request to set `sweep_err` after the read error. The second check requires that request no later than the next cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_32c
          desc: '''A sweep read answered with `d_error` shall raise no alert.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["engine faults have causes (assert_Contracts_EngineFaultsHaveCauses)"]
          why: '''The contract allows the engine's fault inputs to the alert to rise only for their listed causes. A `d_error` on a sweep read is not one of these causes. A design that raises the alert for such an error breaks the contract.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_33a
          desc: '''A response to the engine shall set `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err` when it has an integrity fault, when it is malformed, or when it carries `d_error` and is not the response to a sweep read.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
            '''!!TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["cause sets sweep error (assert_TbreErrors_CauseSetsSweepError)", "error set next cycle (assert_TbreErrors_ErrorSetNextCycle)"]
          why: '''Each cause in the cause table of this testpoint is a cause of the first check, so a cause with no request to set `sweep_err` fails it. The second check requires that request no later than the next cycle. A separate proof reaches malformed answers: it leaves out the TL-UL rules on the opcode and the size of an answer on these ports.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_33b
          desc: '''A response to the engine shall raise `fatal_fault` when it has an integrity fault, when it is malformed, or when it carries `d_error` and is not the response to a sweep read.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
            '''!!TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["bad answer raises fault (assert_TbreErrors_BadAnswerRaisesFault)", "device error raises alert (assert_TagAlerts_DeviceErrorRaisesAlert)"]
          why: '''The first check requires one of the engine's fault inputs to the alert to rise after an answer on `tbre_tl_h` that has an integrity fault or is malformed. An answer that raises none of them fails the first check. A `d_error` on a tag read or a clear raises the alert in the RMW filter, which a check of the tag path decides.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_34a
          desc: '''An answer to a bitmap lookup that carries an error, has an integrity fault or is malformed shall count the capability as revoked.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["revoked gets cleared (assert_TbreDecision_RevokedGetsCleared)"]
          why: '''The definition of revoked includes a capability whose bitmap lookup failed. The check therefore requires a clear for a tagged capability that is not a sealing capability, whose base lies in the main SRAM region and whose lookup failed. A design that keeps the tag of such a capability fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_34b
          desc: '''An answer to a bitmap lookup that carries an error, has an integrity fault or is malformed shall set `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["cause sets sweep error (assert_TbreErrors_CauseSetsSweepError)", "error set next cycle (assert_TbreErrors_ErrorSetNextCycle)"]
          why: '''The first check covers a failed lookup, so a failed lookup with no request to set `sweep_err` fails it. A request that comes later than the next cycle fails the second check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_34c
          desc: '''An answer to a bitmap lookup that carries an error, has an integrity fault or is malformed shall raise `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["bad answer raises fault (assert_TbreErrors_BadAnswerRaisesFault)"]
          why: '''The check requires one of the engine's fault inputs to the alert to rise after any failed lookup. A failed lookup that raises none fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_35a
          desc: '''An RMW filter fault while the engine is active shall set `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
            '''No specification states which faults of the RMW filter count.'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["cause sets sweep error (assert_TbreErrors_CauseSetsSweepError)", "error set next cycle (assert_TbreErrors_ErrorSetNextCycle)"]
          why: '''An RMW filter fault while the engine is active is a cause that the Error Handling table of the theory of operation lists. The check takes every fault that the RMW filter reports.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_35b
          desc: '''An RMW filter fault while the engine is active shall raise `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["RMW fault raises alert (assert_TbreErrors_RmwFaultRaisesAlert)"]
          why: '''The check requires the alert request in the cycle in which an RMW filter fault input rises while the engine is active. A missed alert request fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_36a
          desc: '''`TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err` shall be set only during a sweep, and only by a response to the engine that carries an error, has an integrity fault or is malformed, or by an RMW filter fault.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tbre_errors"
          checks: ["error only for a cause (assert_TbreErrors_ErrorOnlyForACause)"]
          why: '''The check allows a request to set `sweep_err` only while a cause has not yet had one. A request with no cause fails the check. An RMW filter fault while the engine is idle counts as no cause.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_36b
          desc: '''`TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err` shall stay set until software writes 1 to it.'''
          source: [
            '''!!TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The mirror takes the hardware's writes on `hw2reg` and clears the bit only on a software write of 1. A bit that the register file clears on its own fails the comparison. The check does not show that the engine never writes 0 to it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Registers and alert'''
      conditions: [
        '''A row that says a cause raises `fatal_fault` requires an alert event on `alert_tx_o`: a full handshake on the alert pair and the acknowledge pair of the alert handler ([Differential Alert Signaling](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#differential-alert-signaling)).'''
        '''The alert rows hold outside the alert handler's in-band reset ([Employed Solution](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)).'''
        '''A "failed request" is a request whose command integrity code does not match, or a write whose data integrity code does not match ([Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)).'''
        '''No document says whether the data integrity code of a read is checked, so no row covers a read whose only mismatch is that code.'''
        '''A request has an "illegal combination of address, size and mask" when its size is greater than 2, or when its mask has a bit set on an inactive lane ([Explicit Error Cases](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases)).'''
        '''A `PutFullData` request also has an illegal combination when its mask has a 0 on an active lane.'''
        '''`AlertLat` is the number of cycles that the environment allows from a cause, an alert test or a ping to its alert event. No specification gives this number.'''
        '''The Start, status and interrupt group holds the rows of the fields that hardware writes.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_REG_01a
          desc: '''Every register field shall reset to its reset value, as the block description and the register description define it.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `registers`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''[registers.md](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/registers.md)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''After reset, the mirror holds each field's reset value from the register description. The CSR checker compares every field and every read with the mirror, so a field that resets to another value fails the comparison.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_01b
          desc: '''Every register field shall behave as its access type on each software read or write that is answered without an error, as the block description and the register description define it. A write is covered only while the field's `regwen` reads 1, or when the field has no `regwen`.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `registers`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''[registers.md](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/registers.md)'''
            '''[Configuration and Register Definition File Format](util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The mirror updates each field by its access type on every write answered without an error while the field's lock reads 1, and on every hardware write. A field or a read that differs from the mirror fails the comparison.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_02
          desc: '''The register interface shall accept a request at most every other cycle.'''
          source: [
            '''[Revocation Engine](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#revocation-engine)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["request every other cycle (assert_Csr_RequestEveryOtherCycle)"]
          why: '''Two requests that the register interface takes in consecutive cycles fail the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_03a
          desc: '''A software write of 1 to `TBRE_STATUS.start_err` in the cycle in which the engine sets it shall leave `TBRE_STATUS.start_err` clear in the next cycle.'''
          source: [
            '''[Simultaneous SW and HW access](util/reggen/README.md#simultaneous-sw-and-hw-access)'''
            '''!!TBRE_STATUS.start_err'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The mirror applies a software write of 1 after the hardware's set in the same cycle, since the register tool gives software precedence. A bit that is set in the next cycle fails the comparison.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_03b
          desc: '''A software write of 1 to `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err` in the cycle in which the engine sets it shall leave `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err` clear in the next cycle.'''
          source: [
            '''[Simultaneous SW and HW access](util/reggen/README.md#simultaneous-sw-and-hw-access)'''
            '''!!TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The mirror applies a software write of 1 after the hardware's set in the same cycle, since the register tool gives software precedence. A bit that is set in the next cycle fails the comparison.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_04a
          desc: '''Every response of the register interface shall carry the `a_source` of its request as `d_source`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["device rules hold (assert_Bus_DeviceRulesHold)"]
          why: '''The ABVIP compares the `d_source` of each response with the `a_source` of an open request. A response with another source fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_04b
          desc: '''The register interface shall send no response without a request.'''
          source: [
            '''[Response Channel (Channel D)](hw/ip/tlul/doc/TlulProtocolChecker.md#response-channel-channel-d)'''
            '''TileLink specification 1.9.3, section 5.1, page 30'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["device rules hold (assert_Bus_DeviceRulesHold)"]
          why: '''Under the rule `pendingReqPerSrc`, the ABVIP matches each response to an open request with its source. A response with no open request fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_04c
          desc: '''The register interface shall send only one response for each request.'''
          source: [
            '''TileLink specification 1.9.3, section 7, page 46'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["device rules hold (assert_Bus_DeviceRulesHold)"]
          why: '''Under the rule `pendingReqPerSrc`, a response closes its request. A second response then has no open request and fails the rule.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_04d
          desc: '''The register interface shall answer every request that it accepts.'''
          source: [
            '''TileLink specification 1.9.3, section 6.2, page 39'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["accepted request answered (assert_Bus_AcceptedRequestAnswered)"]
          why: '''The check searches for a run in which an accepted request is never answered while the host keeps taking answers. No document gives a bound, so the check has none.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_04e
          desc: '''The register interface shall answer a `Get` with an `AccessAckData`, and every other request with an `AccessAck`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Response Channel (Channel D)](hw/ip/tlul/doc/TlulProtocolChecker.md#response-channel-channel-d)'''
            '''TileLink specification 1.9.3, section 6.2, page 39'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["device rules hold (assert_Bus_DeviceRulesHold)"]
          why: '''Under the rule `respOpcode`, the ABVIP compares each response's `d_opcode` with the opcode that its request needs. A wrong opcode fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_04f
          desc: '''Every response of the register interface shall carry the `a_size` of its request as `d_size`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Response Channel (Channel D)](hw/ip/tlul/doc/TlulProtocolChecker.md#response-channel-channel-d)'''
            '''TileLink specification 1.9.3, section 7.2.4, page 51'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["device rules hold (assert_Bus_DeviceRulesHold)"]
          why: '''Under the rule `d_size`, the ABVIP compares each response's `d_size` with its request's `a_size`. A response with another size fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_05a
          desc: '''A request with an undefined opcode shall receive an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of Opcode, Size and Mask](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-opcode-size-and-mask)'''
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The error check predicts `d_error` 1 for a request with an undefined opcode. The proof lets the opcode take any value.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_05b
          desc: '''A request with an illegal combination of address, size and mask, as the Conditions define it, shall receive an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Explicit Error Cases](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases)'''
            '''[Request Channel (Channel A)](hw/ip/tlul/doc/TlulProtocolChecker.md#request-channel-channel-a)'''
            '''[tl_device_access_types_wo_intg_testplan.hjson](hw/dv/tools/dvsim/testplans/tl_device_access_types_wo_intg_testplan.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The error check predicts `d_error` 1 for each combination that the requirement lists. These combinations include an address that is not aligned to its size.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_05c
          desc: '''A write of 8 or 16 bits to an address that is not word-aligned shall receive an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The error check predicts `d_error` 1 for an 8-bit or 16-bit write to an address that is not word-aligned.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_05d
          desc: '''A write narrower than its register shall receive an error response. The width of a register is set by the location of its fields.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The error check predicts `d_error` 1 for a write narrower than the width that the register's fields set.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_05e
          desc: '''A request to an address that no register maps shall receive an error response, when the address is within the address bits that the register block decodes.'''
          source: [
            '''[Explicit Error Cases](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases)'''
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The error check predicts `d_error` 1 for an address that the register block decodes and no register maps.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_06
          desc: '''A request shall receive an error response only if it is a failed request or a request that one of `REQ_REG_05a` to `REQ_REG_05e` describes. A read whose only mismatch is its data integrity code is not covered.'''
          source: [
            '''[Explicit Error Cases](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases)'''
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''For every request that is not a failed request, the error check requires `d_error` 1 exactly when a cause of `REQ_REG_05a` to `REQ_REG_05e` applies. An error on a request with no such cause fails the check. A failed request is decided by the checks of `bus`. A read whose only mismatch is its data integrity code is not checked.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_07
          desc: '''A failed request shall receive an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
            '''[cip_base_vseq](hw/dv/sv/cip_lib/README.md#cip_base_vseq)'''
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["failed request errors (assert_Bus_FailedRequestErrors)"]
          why: '''The check requires `d_error` 1 on the response to every failed request. A failed request answered without an error fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_08
          desc: '''A write that is a failed request shall change no register.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["failed write changes nothing (assert_Bus_FailedWriteChangesNothing)"]
          why: '''The check requires every field to keep its value over a failed write, apart from a hardware write in that cycle. A failed write that lands fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_09
          desc: '''A write that is answered with an error for any reason other than a failed integrity check shall change no register.'''
          source: [
            '''[Configuration and Register Definition File Format](util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format)'''
            '''[cip_base_vseq](hw/dv/sv/cip_lib/README.md#cip_base_vseq)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The mirror ignores a write answered with an error, so a field that the write changes fails the comparison.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_10a
          desc: '''Every response on `regs_tl_d` shall carry the response integrity code, computed over the opcode, the size and the error of that response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["response codes correct (assert_Bus_ResponseCodesCorrect)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the response integrity code from the response's opcode, size and error, and compares it with the code that the register interface sends.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_10b
          desc: '''Every response on `regs_tl_d` shall carry the data integrity code, computed over the data of that response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["response codes correct (assert_Bus_ResponseCodesCorrect)"]
          why: '''The check recomputes the data integrity code over the response data, and compares it with the code that the register interface sends.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ALT_01
          desc: '''A failed request on `regs_tl_d` shall raise `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["failed request alerts (assert_Alert_FailedRequestAlerts)"]
          why: '''The check requires an alert event within `AlertLat` cycles of every failed request on `regs_tl_d`. A design that answers the request with an error but never signals the alert fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ALT_02
          desc: '''While `ALERT_TEST.regwen` is 1 and no alert handshake is in progress on `alert_tx_o`, a write of 1 to `ALERT_TEST.fatal_fault` that is answered without an error shall send one alert event on `alert_tx_o`.'''
          source: [
            '''!!ALERT_TEST'''
            '''[Test Alert Register Creation](doc/contributing/hw/comportability/README.md#test-alert-register-creation)'''
            '''[alert_test_testplan.hjson](hw/dv/tools/dvsim/testplans/alert_test_testplan.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["test sends an event (assert_Alert_TestSendsAnEvent)", "no alert without a cause (assert_Alert_NoAlertWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''The first check requires an alert event within `AlertLat` cycles of each test write made while no alert handshake is in progress. Outside the fatal state, the second check lets each test write use up one event, so one test write gives one event.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ALT_03a
          desc: '''Once software writes 0 to `ALERT_TEST.regwen`, `ALERT_TEST.regwen` shall read 0 until reset.'''
          source: [
            '''!!ALERT_TEST'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The mirror holds `ALERT_TEST.regwen` as an `rw0c` field: a write of 0 clears it and nothing sets it before reset. A lock that reads 1 again fails the comparison.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ALT_03b
          desc: '''Once software writes 0 to `ALERT_TEST.regwen`, a write to `ALERT_TEST.fatal_fault` that is not a failed request shall cause no alert event on `alert_tx_o` until reset.'''
          source: [
            '''!!ALERT_TEST'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["no alert without a cause (assert_Alert_NoAlertWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''A write to `ALERT_TEST.fatal_fault` after software wrote 0 to `ALERT_TEST.regwen` adds no credit. An alert event outside the fatal state with no ping credit then fails the check.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ALT_03c
          desc: '''`ALERT_TEST.regwen` shall read 1 after reset.'''
          source: [
            '''!!ALERT_TEST'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "csr"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''After reset, the mirror holds the reset value 1. A lock at 0 fails the comparison.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ALT_06
          desc: '''The subsystem shall answer each ping of the alert handler on `alert_rx_i` with one alert event on `alert_tx_o`.'''
          source: [
            '''[Ping Testing](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#ping-testing)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["ping answered (assert_Alert_PingAnswered)", "no alert without a cause (assert_Alert_NoAlertWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''The first check requires an alert event within `AlertLat` cycles of each ping. Outside the fatal state, the second check lets each ping use up one event, so one ping gives one event.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''End-to-end requirements'''
      conditions: [
        '''The rows state end-to-end behaviour that no single checker decides.'''
        '''Each row follows from the checks of several checkers, and from the assumption that the meta SRAM returns, for a read, the word last written to that address.'''
        '''A tag write starts with a `Get` of the meta word. The tag rows `REQ_TAG_01` to `REQ_TAG_04` and the sweep row `REQ_TBRE_38` hold from reset until the answer to such a `Get` has a broken integrity code and no `d_error`.'''
        '''From that answer on, the plan claims nothing about the tags.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_01
          desc: '''A hinted capability load in CHERIoT mode shall return the tag last written to that capability through the tag path, in the order in which tag writes reach the meta SRAM. A write that an error aborts writes nothing. A load of a capability never written shall return the meta SRAM's starting content.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TAG_READ`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TAG_SPLIT`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_read_after_write"
          checks: ["tag word and bit (assert_TfMetaRequest_TagWordAndBit)", "answer tag follows rule (assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule)", "keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)", "from the named input (assert_ArbForward_FromTheNamedInput)", "core request unchanged (assert_ArbForward_CoreRequestUnchanged)", "answer to its input (assert_ArbReturn_AnswerToItsInput)", "taken with its input (assert_ArbReturn_TakenWithItsInput)", "fields unchanged (assert_ArbReturn_FieldsUnchanged)", "Get of its meta word (assert_RmwRead_GetOfItsMetaWord)", "returns its tag bit (assert_RmwRead_ReturnsItsTagBit)", "carries the updated word (assert_RmwWriteBack_CarriesTheUpdatedWord)", "one operation at a time (assert_RmwSingleOp_OneOperationAtATime)", "nothing else downstream (assert_RmwSingleOp_NothingElseDownstream)", "legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)", "no extra meta SRAM request (assert_MetaForward_NoExtraMetaSramRequest)", "answer to its port (assert_MetaReturn_AnswerToItsPort)", "source shifted back (assert_MetaReturn_SourceShiftedBack)", "fields unchanged (assert_MetaReturn_FieldsUnchanged)", "taken with its port (assert_MetaReturn_TakenWithItsPort)", "only the meta SRAM's answer (assert_MetaReturn_OnlyTheMetaSRAMsAnswer)", "other ports never reach tags (assert_TagIsolation_OtherPortsNeverReachTags)"]
          why: '''The tag path checker proves that the tag filter asks for the right word and bit and returns the tag of the meta answer. It also proves that the 2:1 tag arbiter passes each request on unchanged and returns each answer to its input. Finally, it proves that the RMW filter reads and writes only that bit, one operation at a time. The meta access checker proves that the tag port passes those requests to the meta SRAM unchanged, and that no other port reaches the tag words. The meta SRAM keeps what it is given (an assumption of the plan), so the tag read back is the one last written.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_02
          desc: '''A write to the main SRAM in CHERIoT mode shall set the addressed capability's tag to the write's tag sideband. A non-capability write therefore clears the tag.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TAG_CLEAR_ON_DATA_WRITE`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''CHERIoT architecture specification v1.0, section 7.7'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_read_after_write"
          checks: ["lookup in same cycle (assert_TfLookup_LookupInSameCycle)", "no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)", "tag word and bit (assert_TfMetaRequest_TagWordAndBit)", "write carries its tag (assert_TfMetaRequest_WriteCarriesItsTag)", "Get only for a read (assert_TfMetaRequest_GetOnlyForARead)", "keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)", "from the named input (assert_ArbForward_FromTheNamedInput)", "core request unchanged (assert_ArbForward_CoreRequestUnchanged)", "full-word Get first (assert_RmwWriteSkip_FullWordGetFirst)", "answer after Get answer (assert_RmwWriteSkip_AnswerAfterGetAnswer)", "carries the updated word (assert_RmwWriteBack_CarriesTheUpdatedWord)", "full-word Put to same word (assert_RmwWriteBack_FullWordPutToSameWord)", "nothing else downstream (assert_RmwSingleOp_NothingElseDownstream)", "legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)", "no extra meta SRAM request (assert_MetaForward_NoExtraMetaSramRequest)"]
          why: '''The tag filter looks up every write once, at the right word and bit, with the write's tag sideband as the tag. The 2:1 tag arbiter passes this meta request on unchanged. The RMW filter reads the word first and then writes it back with that bit set to the tag. The tag port passes the write-back to the meta SRAM unchanged. A non-capability write carries tag 0 in its tag sideband, so it clears the tag.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_03
          desc: '''A plain store or an untagged capability store to the NVM shall clear the addressed capability's tag.'''
          source: [
            '''[Storing Capabilities in the NVM](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#storing-capabilities-in-the-nvm)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_read_after_write"
          checks: ["lookup in same cycle (assert_TfLookup_LookupInSameCycle)", "no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)", "tag word and bit (assert_TfMetaRequest_TagWordAndBit)", "write carries its tag (assert_TfMetaRequest_WriteCarriesItsTag)", "Get only for a read (assert_TfMetaRequest_GetOnlyForARead)", "keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)", "from the named input (assert_ArbForward_FromTheNamedInput)", "core request unchanged (assert_ArbForward_CoreRequestUnchanged)", "full-word Get first (assert_RmwWriteSkip_FullWordGetFirst)", "answer after Get answer (assert_RmwWriteSkip_AnswerAfterGetAnswer)", "carries the updated word (assert_RmwWriteBack_CarriesTheUpdatedWord)", "full-word Put to same word (assert_RmwWriteBack_FullWordPutToSameWord)", "nothing else downstream (assert_RmwSingleOp_NothingElseDownstream)", "legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)", "no extra meta SRAM request (assert_MetaForward_NoExtraMetaSramRequest)"]
          why: '''A plain store and an untagged capability store to the NVM both carry tag 0 in their tag sideband. A capability store to the NVM is a write with the tag sideband set, so neither of these stores is a capability store to the NVM. Each of them therefore needs a lookup, and the same chain as for `REQ_TAG_02` writes tag 0.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_04
          desc: '''A tag write shall change no other capability's tag.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TAG_WRITE_RMW`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_read_after_write"
          checks: ["tag word and bit (assert_TfMetaRequest_TagWordAndBit)", "keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)", "core request unchanged (assert_ArbForward_CoreRequestUnchanged)", "carries the updated word (assert_RmwWriteBack_CarriesTheUpdatedWord)", "nothing else downstream (assert_RmwSingleOp_NothingElseDownstream)", "legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)", "no extra meta SRAM request (assert_MetaForward_NoExtraMetaSramRequest)", "other ports never reach tags (assert_TagIsolation_OtherPortsNeverReachTags)"]
          why: '''The write-back of the RMW filter keeps every other bit of its word, and it is the only write that the RMW filter sends. The tag port passes the write-back unchanged, and no other port reaches the tag words. Therefore no other capability's tag changes.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TAG_09
          desc: '''Every core request shall be answered, whatever requests the revocation engine's tag filter makes on the shared RMW filter. The requirement holds provided that `xbar_main` and the meta SRAM answer their requests.'''
          source: [
            '''[Tag Filter](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#tag-filter)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "tag_no_deadlock"
          checks: ["meta answer taken (assert_TfFlow_MetaAnswerTaken)", "request eventually accepted (assert_TfFlow_RequestEventuallyAccepted)", "request eventually answered (assert_TfFlow_RequestEventuallyAnswered)", "no starvation (assert_ArbFlow_NoStarvation)", "one answer per operation (assert_RmwSingleOp_OneAnswerPerOperation)", "every operation answered (assert_RmwSingleOp_EveryOperationAnswered)", "access request accepted and answered (assert_Contracts_AccessRequestAcceptedAndAnswered)", "engine meta answer taken (assert_Contracts_EngineMetaAnswerTaken)"]
          why: '''The core's tag filter always takes its meta answers, so a meta answer never waits for a data answer. The 2:1 tag arbiter starves neither of its inputs. The RMW filter answers every operation. The access checkers accept requests and answer them, and the engine's tag filter takes its meta answers. Therefore no core request waits forever.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: its checks follow the fairness of the 2:1 tag arbiter, which no specification states"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_38
          desc: '''After a sweep during which no error set `TBRE_STATUS.sweep_err`, every swept capability that was revoked when the engine read it, and that no core write touched in its watch window, shall read back untagged until it is written again.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TBRE_SWEEP`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
            '''[Tracking Completed Sweeps](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/programmers_guide.md#tracking-completed-sweeps)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rev_end_to_end"
          checks: ["revoked gets cleared (assert_TbreDecision_RevokedGetsCleared)", "clears tracked bit once (assert_TbreClear_ClearsTrackedBitOnce)", "writes tag 0 (assert_TbreClear_WritesTag0)", "fresh clear stays write (assert_TbreWatch_FreshClearStaysWrite)", "keeps its own sideband (assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband)", "from the named input (assert_ArbForward_FromTheNamedInput)", "full-word Get first (assert_RmwWriteSkip_FullWordGetFirst)", "answer after Get answer (assert_RmwWriteSkip_AnswerAfterGetAnswer)", "carries the updated word (assert_RmwWriteBack_CarriesTheUpdatedWord)", "full-word Put to same word (assert_RmwWriteBack_FullWordPutToSameWord)", "legal request forwarded (assert_MetaForward_LegalRequestForwarded)", "no extra meta SRAM request (assert_MetaForward_NoExtraMetaSramRequest)"]
          why: '''The engine clears every capability that was revoked when it was read. Each clear is a write of tag 0 to the capability's tag bit, and it stays a write while no core write touches the capability. The 2:1 tag arbiter and the RMW filter turn the clear into a write-back of that bit alone. The tag port passes the write-back to the meta SRAM unchanged. The meta SRAM keeps what it is given (an assumption of the plan), so the capability reads back untagged until it is written again.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_TBRE_39
          desc: '''A capability that a core write touched in its watch window shall keep the tag that write gave it.'''
          source: [
            '''[cheriot_mem_sys.hjson `TBRE_CORE_WRITE_SNOOP`](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/data/cheriot_mem_sys.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "rev_end_to_end"
          checks: ["clear only if untouched (assert_TbreWatch_ClearOnlyIfUntouched)", "stale clear becomes read (assert_TbreWatch_StaleClearBecomesRead)", "clear held unchanged (assert_TbreWatch_ClearHeldUnchanged)", "lookup in same cycle (assert_TfLookup_LookupInSameCycle)", "forwarded unchanged (assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged)", "alone in same cycle (assert_ArbFlow_AloneInSameCycle)", "one operation at a time (assert_RmwSingleOp_OneOperationAtATime)", "nothing else downstream (assert_RmwSingleOp_NothingElseDownstream)"]
          why: '''The core's tag filter looks up the core's write and forwards it unchanged, and the write then passes the 2:1 tag arbiter. The RMW filter does one operation at a time, so no other operation splits the core's tag write. A clear that the core's write overtakes is not presented, or it reaches the RMW filter as a read. A clear that is already at the RMW filter is held there. The RMW filter writes nothing for a read, so the tag that the core wrote stays.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ALT_04
          desc: '''The subsystem shall raise no alert for a meta SRAM access in ePMP mode, for an access outside the region of its port, or for a `PutPartialData` to the meta SRAM.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["no alert without a cause (assert_Alert_NoAlertWithoutACause)", "alert only on a fault (assert_AlertCauses_AlertOnlyOnAFault)", "tag path faults have causes (assert_Contracts_TagPathFaultsHaveCauses)", "engine faults have causes (assert_Contracts_EngineFaultsHaveCauses)", "no unneeded lookup (assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup)", "tag word and bit (assert_TfMetaRequest_TagWordAndBit)", "Get of its meta word (assert_RmwRead_GetOfItsMetaWord)", "full-word Get first (assert_RmwWriteSkip_FullWordGetFirst)", "full-word Put to same word (assert_RmwWriteBack_FullWordPutToSameWord)", "tag filter checks hold (assert_TbreClear_TagFilterChecksHold)", "engine addresses whole words (assert_Contracts_EngineAddressesWholeWords)"]
          why: '''An alert event needs the fatal state or a credit. The fatal state needs a failed request or a raised fault input. Each fault input rises only for its listed causes. The three refusals that the requirement names are not among these causes. A refusal of a tag path request would come back to the RMW filter as a device error, which raises the alert. These checks show that the tag path asks only in CHERIoT mode, inside the tag port's region, for whole words, and never with a `PutPartialData`. The tag access checker therefore refuses none of the tag path's requests.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ALT_05
          desc: '''Outside the alert handler's in-band reset, the subsystem shall send an alert event on `alert_tx_o` only after a cause that the Error Handling table lists with the alert, after an alert test or in answer to a ping. A read on `regs_tl_d` whose only mismatch is its data integrity code is not covered.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error Handling](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/theory_of_operation.md#error-handling)'''
            '''[Security Alerts](hw/ip/cheriot_mem_sys/doc/interfaces.md#security-alerts)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["no alert without a cause (assert_Alert_NoAlertWithoutACause)", "alert only on a fault (assert_AlertCauses_AlertOnlyOnAFault)", "tag path faults have causes (assert_Contracts_TagPathFaultsHaveCauses)", "engine faults have causes (assert_Contracts_EngineFaultsHaveCauses)", "invalid tag fault has a cause (assert_TagAlerts_InvalidTagFaultHasACause)"]
          why: '''The checks tie each alert event to a failed request, a fault input, a test write or a ping. They also tie each fault input to its causes. The last check ties the fault input of an invalid tag sideband to its causes. A design that sends an alert event with no cause fails one of these links. A read whose only mismatch is its data integrity code is left out, as the requirement says.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: no check ties the fault input of an invalid tag sideband to its cause"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
